3 CONC our 29th great grandfathe
2 NOTE The Irish record of The Mothers of the Irish Saints is found in the Books of Leinster, Ballymote, Lecan and Uí Maine. They list the following sons by Brychan's wife, Dína daughter of the King of the Saxons:
3 CONT
3 CONT Mo-Goróc
3 CONT Mo-Chonóc
3 CONT
3 CONT (Cynog)
3 CONT
3 CONT Diraid
3 CONT
3 CONT Dubán
3 CONT
3 CONT (Dyfnan)
3 CONT
3 CONT Cairinne
3 CONT
3 CONT (Caian)
3 CONT
3 CONT Cairpre
3 CONT
3 CONT Iast
3 CONT
3 CONT Ellóc
3 CONT
3 CONT (Dilic)
3 CONT
3 CONT Paan
3 CONT
3 CONT Cáemán
3 CONT
3 CONT Mo-Beóc
3 CONT
3 CONT Breton Tradition says that Brychan married Menedoc daughter of Constantine, King of the Scots. Together they were the parents of:
3 CONT
3 CONT Nennocha
