1 NOTE LORD OF BRECKNOCK
1 NOTE 1  NAME Brychan /Brycheiniog/ 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001 1  DEAT 2  DATE ABT. 450 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Ireland but soon his parents moved to Wales.  Was the King of Garthmadryn, which was later called Brecknockafter him.  Many of his children had the reputation of great sanctity and preached the Gospel to the Britions who h
2 CONC ad relapsed into paganism [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Brychan Brycheiniog was the King of Garthmadryn, which was later called Brycheiniog or Brecknock after him.  He began his reign about 400, and died about 450. He married and had numerous issue. Many of his children had the reputat
2 CONC ion of great sanctity and preached the Gospel to the Britons who had relapsed into paganism.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT   Source not indicated.
