2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Maximus alias Macsen Wledig (the Imperator), Emperor of the West, Abt 340 - 388
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Ceindrech ferch Reiden
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Victor alias Gwidyr, Abt 354 - 388
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Eugenius alias Owain Finddu (Black Lips), King of 
2 CONT   Mid-South Wales, Abt 355 -
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT m. St. Helena of the Host, alias Elen Lwyddog, daughter of Octavius the Old alias Eudaf Hen, Abt 340
2 CONT Saint Elen Luyddog ferch Eudaf (cca 340- 388 Udine)
2 CONT
2 CONT *. Antoninus Donatus alias Anwn Dynod, King of 
2 CONT     South-West Wales, Abt 357 -
2 CONT
2 CONT *. Constantine alias Custennin Fawr (the Great), King 
2 CONT     of North-West Wales, Abt 360 -
2 CONT
2 CONT *. Publicus alias St. Peblig of Llanbeblig, Abt 363 -
2 CONT
2 CONT *. Gratianna, Abt 367 - , m. Tudwal ap Gwrfawr, King of 
2 CONT     Dumnonia, Abt 375 -
2 CONT
2 CONT *. Severa, Abt 370 - , m. Vortigern Vorteneu (the Thin), 
2 CONT     King of Powys & All Britain, Abt 370 - Abt 459
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Then there was Coel Godhebog (the Magnificent), traditionally a 'dux' of Camelodunum (Colchester); probably a decurion in fact. He supposedly lived in the 3rd century and his daughter, St. Helena of Colchester, married the Roman E
2 CONC mperor, Constantius Chlorus. They may have been the ancestors of Magnus Maximus.
2 CONT ----------   
