2 CONT Magnus Clemens Maximus d. 388, Roman emperor of the West (383-388). After his followers murdered Gratian , he was recognized as ruler of Britain, Gaul, and Spain by Theodosius I . He invaded Italy in 387, expelling Valentinian II 
2 CONC , but the following year he was defeated and put to death by Theodosius. In the reign of Maximus the heresy of Priscillian was suppressed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Author not available, MAXIMUS, MAGNUS CLEMENS., The Columbia Encyclopedia, Sixth Edition 2007
