2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Constantine''' (Welsh, '''Custennyn map Macsen'''), born, say about 360, the son of Roman usurper [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-II-Macsen-Wledig-Roman-Usurper/5365308074870051638 Magnus Clemens Maximus] (Welsh, "Macsen Gwl
2 CONC edig"), executed in 388. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Later legend confuses this Constantine with his namesake [http://www.geni.com/people/Constantine-I-the-Great-Roman-Emperor/6000000002119283341 Constantine the Great], Emperor of Rome. The confusion seems to have arisen because of 
2 CONC a confusion between their mothers, [http://www.geni.com/people/St-Elen-Lwyddog-of-the-Host-of-Britain/377649183480004232 St. Elen Luyddog] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Helena-of-the-Cross/6000000002122805101 St. Helen of 
2 CONC the Cross]. However, this Constantine lived at least a generation later than Constantine the Great. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to one tradition, he was the Constantine who was father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Aurelianus-Ambrosius/6000000006290723855 Ambrosius] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Uther-Ottar-Dragebane/6000000003827288024 Uther P
2 CONC endragon]. Some contemporary scholars speculate he might have been identical with Roman usurper [http://www.geni.com/people/Constantine-III-Western-Roman-Emperor/6000000002188327480 Constantine III], executed in 411.
