1 NAME Madrun /verch Vortimer/
2 GIVN Madrun
2 SURN verch Vortimer
2 _MARNM verch Vortimer
2 NICK Madrun
2 NICK Madryn
1 NAME Saint Madrun verch Vortimer
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 450
1 OCCU Saint
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392786891 (February 6, 2023; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Composite Lives of St Beuno; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id23.html. (Steven Ferry, February 19, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Another Look at Teithfallt of Gwent; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id168.html. (Steven Ferry, February 25, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Her handmaiden was St. Anhun.  She was the daughter of King Vortimer Fendigaid. Married to Prince Ynyr. Queen of Gwent. While on pilgrimage, she received a dream in which she was told to build a convent where she slept; the church
2 CONC  there has survived to today. Mother of Saint Ceidio; she helped him evangelize the area around Minster in Cornwall. Widow.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Wikipedia (22 Apr 2022) [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Materiana Saint Materiana – Alternative spellings are Madrun and Madryn]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.catholic.org/saints/saint.php?saint_id=4408
