2 CONT http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per08788.htm#0	
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cunedda was also called Cunedag. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Chronicle of Ystrad Fflur (400): "In this year Cunedda, Kaletach wrth elyn nac asgwrn, and his sons came from Manaw Gododdin to expel the Irish."
2 CONT
2 CONT Cunedda Wledig ab Edeyrn of Britain married Gwawl verch Coel of Britain, daughter of Dux Britanniarium Coel Hen Guotepauk of Britain and Ystradwal verch Cadfan o Dumnonia, before 417.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Pictish chief of the Manaw Gododdin, a subsidiary of the main Gododdin people who lay just beyond the Antonine Wall, around the Forth's headwaters and a natural citadel at Stirling, before 424 at Lothian, Scotland. He w
2 CONC as invited by Magnus Maximus to settle in northwest Wales circa 424.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cunedda was our ancestor through two distinct lines of descent--through his son Brenin and his daughter Gwen, each of whom was independently our ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p91.htm#i11473 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The wikipedia entry is here http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cunedda
2 CONT
2 CONT ca 5th Century
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Came from Manaw Gododin on the Firth of forth.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cunedda ap Edern (c. 386–c. 460 AD; reigned from the 440s or 450s) (Latin: Cunetacius; English: Kenneth), also known as Cunedda Wledig ("holder of lands"), was an important early Welsh leader, and the progenitor of the royal dynas
2 CONC ty of Gwynedd.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cunedda Wledig or Cynedda Weledit or Kenneth The Warrior or Guledig ap Edern.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT A northern British chieftain who ruled part of Gododdin. He and his warband rode across Britain to help expel Irish invaders from Wales. He settled down in Gwynedd and founded a number of royal dynasties.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Wledig means "holder of lands." Cunedda derives from the Brythonic word kunodagos, meaning "good hound."
2 CONT
2 CONT An important early Welsh leader, and the progenitor of the royal dynasty of Gwynedd.
2 CONT
2 CONT See: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cunedda
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT By the time Rome left Britain in the early 5th century, two branches were seated in the far north (Cunedda and Coel Hen) and two in what is now Powys (Gwrtheyrn aka Vortigern and Cadell).  Cunedda relocated to Gwynedd where his fa
2 CONC mily had intermarried with men descended from Llyr Llediath and he was the founder of the First Royal Dynasty of Gwynedd.  Men descended from Coel Hen were called "The Men of The North" and they did not migrate to Wales until the 
2 CONC Saxons forced them from their lands in the 7th century.  A man of that line founded the Second Royal Dynasty of Gwynedd in the 9th century.  We think a double marriage united the two Powys families in the 5th century; the First Po
2 CONC wys Dynasty was descended from Cadell Ddyrnllwg, while the Second Powys Dynasty descended from Cassanauth Wledig, a man we believe was a grandson of Gwrtheyrn (Vortigern).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT aka the progenitor of the Gwynedd dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Known as "the great".
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p638.htm#i19153
2 CONT
2 CONT Cunedda ap Edern , även kallad Cunedda Wledig (regerade ca  450 - ca 460), var en viktig tidig walesisk ledare och stamfadern till den kungliga dynastin Gwynedd , en av de allra äldsta i Västeuropa . [ 1 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Namn
2 CONT Se även: Wledig
2 CONT Namnet Cunedda (stavat Cunedag i pseudohistorien Historia Brittonum e.Kr. 828 ) härstammar från det Brythonic ordet * Cuno-dagos , som betyder "bra hund/krigare" eller "att ha bra hundar/krigare". [ 2 ] Hans titel, " Wledig ", är 
2 CONC en obskyr och svåröversatt epitet . [ 3 ] Det betyder ordagrant, "av en gwlad " eller "land". [ 3 ] Emellertid, som ett epitet, applicerades Wledig möjligen på någon officiell eller påstådd position inom den romerska hierarkin. [ 
2 CONC 3 ] Det har hävdats att termen sannolikt är en återgivning av en romersk titel eftersom alla kända figurer med titeln antingen är genealogiskt kopplade till den romerska aristokratin eller förknippade med den romerska regeringen. 
2 CONC [ 3 ] [ 4 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dessa figurer härskade också alla under århundradet efter det romerska tillbakadragandet från Storbritannien. Denna tolkning är dock föremål för kritik. Historikern Rachel Bromwich hävdade att översättning av latinska titlar till 
2 CONC walesiska är ovanligt för samtida walesiska ledare, som vanligtvis använde de ursprungliga latinska titlarna. [ 5 ] Det finns andra konkurrerande teorier om den sanna innebörden av begreppet. Ordet " Gwledig " är ett besläktat med
2 CONC  det irländska ordet " flaith ", som betyder linjal. Därför kan ordet helt enkelt betyda "herre" eller "härskare". [ 6 ]
