1 NOTE OR "MEIRCHIAWNGUL"
1 NOTE Welsh" Meirchion; Latin: Marcianus; English: Mark
2 CONT
2 CONT Meirchion "the Lean", presumably a very slim man, was King of a united Rheged, though he lost Elmet to his younger brother, Mascuid. Upon Meirchion's death in about 535, the Kingdom was divided between his two sons.
