1 NOTE PRINCE OF STRATHCLYDE.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://awt.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:1538846&id=I20157
1 NOTE PRINCE OF STRATHCLYDE
1 NOTE Welsh: Elidyr; Latin: Elidurus; English: Elider
2 CONT
2 CONT The first King of Rheged's southern region covering modern Lancashire and Cheshire, and probably centered on Ribchester or Lancaster. Rheged-dale or modern Rochdale still retains the name of his Kingdom. Little is known ablout him
2 CONC , unlike his contemporary and namesake with whom he is often confused, the Strathclyde Prince, Elidyr Mwynfawr "The Wealthy". The King of South Rheged was Stout and Hamdsome.
