1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Kraentzler 1750; History of Morgan Family.   History: Cadwallon Lawhir, the Long-Handed, was the father of Maelgwn Gwynned.    AF record says he was King of North Wales.
2 CONT    K: Caswallawn Lawhir, expelled the Irish from Anglesey.                     ******** Cadwallon Lawhir, the Long-Handed, was the father of Maelgwn Gwynedd.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT   1.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.
