2 CONT
2 CONT ^ a b c MacQuarrie, p. 5.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Koch, p. 458.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Bromwich, p. 314.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ N. J. Lacy, A history of Arthurian scholarship Arthurian studies, 65 (Boydell & Brewer Ltd, 2006), pp. 9-10.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Morris, p. 54
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Henry of Huntingdon, Historia Anglorum, Book I, ch. 37.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Greenway, pp. 60–61.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ a b Greenway, p. civ.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ a b Thorpe, p. 17; 131.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Harbus, p. 74.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT Bromwich, Rachel (2006). Trioedd Ynys Prydein: The Triads of the Island of Britain. University Of Wales Press. ISBN 0-7083-1386-8.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greenway, Diana (Ed.); Henry of Huntingdon (1996). Historia Anglorum: The History of the English People. Oxford University Press. ISBN 0198222246.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harbus, A. (2002). Helena of Britain in Medieval Legend. D. S. Brewer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Koch, John T. (2006). Celtic Culture: A Historical Encyclopedia. ABC-CLIO. ISBN 1851094407.
2 CONT
2 CONT MacQuarrie, Alan; A. Grant & K. Stringer (Eds.) (1993). "The Kings of Strathclyde". Medieval Scotland: Crown, Lordship and Community (Edinburgh University Press): 1–19.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris, John (1973). The Age of Arthur. London: Weidenfeld & Nicolson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Opie, I.; Opie, P. (1997). The Oxford Dictionary of Nursery Rhymes. Oxford University Press.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorpe, Lewis (Ed.); Geoffrey of Monmouth (1966). The History of the Kings of Britain. London: Penguin. ISBN 0-14-044170-0.
2 CONT
