2 CONT Sources: Kings and Queens of Britain; Kraentzler 1749; History of Morgan Family.
2 CONT    K and Q: Cadwallon ap Cadfan, King of Gwynedd.   History: King of Gwynedd 616. Cadfan ap Iago is buried at Llangadwaladr, and his tombstone is inscribed "King Cadfan, most wide, most renowned." One of his sons was Cadwallon. K:
2 CONC  spells burial place Llancadwalladr.   K: Cadvan or Catgublawn, King of West Wales, Britain. Died 634. Slain at Catiscaul. Kraentzler says he married a daughter of Penda, undoubtedly an error because a sister or half-sister of Pen
2 CONC da married Cadwallon, son of Cadfan.                           ****** King of Gwynedd, 616.  Cadfan ap Iago is buried at Llangadwaladr and his tombstone is inscribed "King Cadfan, most wide, most renowned."  One of his sons was Ca
2 CONC swallon.  Other sources call him Cadfan/Cadvar, King of Venedoti and South Britain, c. 616-617.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT   1.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.
