1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aethelwald is Son of Saint Oswald, King of Northumbria and Cyneburg.The former goes back to Kings Ida and Eoppa of Northumbria. The latter is a daughter of the lines descending from the House of Wessex. St. Oswald 
2 CONC attended the baptism of King of Wessex, Cynegils, as his godfather in 635 and then Cynegils gave his daughter Cyneburh to marry St. Oswald upon the occasion of his becoming a Christian (Cynegils). See:
2 CONT https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PL_pHinx0Ms for information on the marriage of St. Oswald and Cyneburh as well as the son of the marriage, Aethelwald.(at just before minute 7). The same Youtube url also states that Aethelwald in 1
2 CONC 651 was crowned King of Deira and then had a short reign until 654 although he was said to be too young to rule.
