1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Augustine of Hipp,o Latin: Aurelius Augustinus Hipponensis; 13 November 354 – 28 August 430), also known as St Augustine, St Austin, or St Augoustinos, was a Father of the Church whose writings are considered very 
2 CONC influential in the development of Western Christianity and philosophy. He was bishop of Hippo Regius (present-day Annaba, Algeria) of the Roman province of Africa. He belongs to Haplogroup E-M35
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustine_of_Hippo
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine of Hippo (/ɔːˈɡʌstɪn/ aw-GUST-in, US also /ˈɔːɡəstiːn/ AW-gə-steen;[22] Latin: Aurelius Augustinus Hipponensis; 13 November 354 – 28 August 430),[23] also known as Saint Augustine, was a theologian and philosopher of Ber
2 CONC ber origin and the bishop of Hippo Regius in Numidia, Roman North Africa. His writings influenced the development of Western philosophy and Western Christianity, and he is viewed as one of the most important Church Fathers of the 
2 CONC Latin Church in the Patristic Period. His many important works include The City of God, On Christian Doctrine, and Confessions.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/augustine/
2 CONT * https://hymnary.org/person/Augustine_Saint
