1 NOTE KNOWN AS "CLORUS"; AN ILLYRIAN; ROMAN EMPORER (CAESAR 293, AUGUSTUS 305)
1 NOTE His full name is Flavius Valerius Constantius, called Constantius Chlorus. 
2 CONT  He was a general and administrator under Emperor Maximian, who adopted 
2 CONT him and gave him the government of Gaul and the rank of caesar in 293. 
2 CONT When his coemperors, Maximian and Diocletian, abdicated in 305, 
2 CONT Constantius became emperor in the West and prepared to conquer the Picts 
2 CONT of Scotland. He died during the campaign, after proclaiming his son 
2 CONT Constantine his successor as emperor.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
2 CONT Original individual @P2203775237@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@) merged with @P2203775113@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@)
1 NOTE SOME SOURCES SAY GAIUS'S PARENTS WERE EUTROPIUS (NOTES) OR FLAVIUS ( L) DE ROME AND CLAUDIA CRISPINA (L) ILLYRIA
2 CONT
2 CONT OTHER POSSIBLE PARENTS ARE SHOWN BELOW BUT THIS INDIVIDUAL IS NOT SHO WN AS A CHILD ON THE FOLLOWING POSSIBLE PARENTS' FAMILY PAGES,  TO DO SO W OULD BE  CONSIDERED ERRORS BY THIS PROGRAM.  EVEN THOUGH THESE LAST POSSIB LE PARENTS
2 CONC  MAY BE THE CORRECT ONES, SHOWING MORE THAN ONE SET OF PARENTS C OULD CAUSE MY "FAMILY TREE" PROGRAM TO MALFUNCTION.
2 CONT
2 CONT OTHER SOURCES SAY HIS FATHER WAS EUTROPIUS (NOTES) OF (L) DARDANIA ANOTH ER OF HIS MOTHER CLAUDIA'S HUSBANDS.
2 CONT
2 CONT STILL OTHER SOURCES SAY HIS PARENTS WERE COLIUS II (NOTES) "OLD KING COL E" (L) COLCHESTER AND STRADA YSTRADWEL (NOTES) VERCH (L) CADFAN AND HIS SI STER WAS THEN HELENA "SAINT" (NOTE)OF THE CROSS (L) COLCHESTERWHILE STI LL OTHER S
2 CONC OURCES SAY HIS WIFE WAS (HIS SISTER?) THE SAME.HELENA "SAINT" (N OTE)OF THE CROSS (L) COLCHESTER.
2 CONT
2 CONT I SHOW HELENA AS HIS WIFE NOT AS HIS SISTER HERE.
2 CONT
