1 NOTE  ANNA (-killed in battle 654).  Bede names Anna, son of Enni "of the blood royal", as successor of Ecgric and "father of an excellent family of children"[59].  William of Malmesbury names Anna as sonof Enni and successor of Ecgric
2 CONC [60].  He succeeded in 635 as ANNA King of the East Angles.  After his expulsion from Wessex in 645 by Penda King of Mercia, Cenwalh King of Wessex sought refuge with King Anna whose influence may have caused him to accept baptism
2 CONC  in 646.  Penda of Mercia attacked East Anglia in [650], destroyed the monastery of Cnobheresburg (possibly Burgh Castle, Norfolk) and expelled King Anna temporarily.  Bede specifies that King Anna was "also slain by the same paga
2 CONC n commander as his predecessor had been"[61].  The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle records that "king Anna was killed"in 653/54, but gives no details[62].  [m firstly --- .  As noted below, the difference between the estimated birth dates o
2 CONC f King Anna's two daughters suggests that he may have been married twice.]  m[secondly] ([635 or after]) as her second husband, ---.  The name of the wife of King Anna is not known.  The fact that this was her second marriage is d
2 CONC educed from Bede naming "Sethrid daughter of the wife of Anna king of the East Angles" among those sent to France "to the monasteries of Brie, Chelles and Andelys" to be instructed "and delivered to their heavenly bridegroom", spe
2 CONC cifying that shebecame abbess of the "monastery of Brie" [Faremoutiers-en-Brie][63].  If the details are correct, Bede must be referring to King Anna's second wife (assuming that it is correct that he was married twice).  The name
2 CONC  "Sethrid" appears to be composed of root elements similar to those in names of the kings of the East Saxons (Essex).  This recalls the East Saxon sounding name of King Anna's predecessor, King Sigeberht.  Is it therefore possible
2 CONC  that King Anna married the widow of his predecessor but one in order to affirm his position as ruler in East Anglia after 635?  If this is correct, it mayhave been his second marriage in view of the estimated birth date of his da
2 CONC ughter Seaxburh (see below).
