1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Eomer / Ēomǣr''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King of the Angles, Germany ~~ see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kings_of_the_Angles#Angeltheow
2 CONT ==========
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the ''Anglo-Saxon Chronicle'', he was the great-great-grandfather of Creoda 1st King of Mercia. He is considered the ancestral patriarch to the Kings of Mercia. 
2 CONT Eomer himself was the son of Angeltheow (Offa of Angel). 
2 CONT Eomer's son was Icel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is mentioned in lines 1958 thru 1963 of the Anglo-Saxon ''Epic of Beowulf'' as the son of Offa of Angel and grandson of Garmund.
2 CONT
2 CONT "...forþam Offa wæs geofum and guðum gar-cene man, wide geweorðod; wisdome heold eðel sinne, þonon Eomær woc hæleðum to helpe, Heminges mæg, nefa Garmundes, niða cræftig."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Hence Offa was praised for his fighting and feeing by far-off men, the spear-bold warrior; wisely he ruled over his empire. Eomer woke to him, help of heroes, Hemming's kinsman, Grandson of Garmund, grim in war."
2 CONT (Gummere's translation)   
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_of_the_Angles
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Emeric von Angeln, Kg. d. Angeln, geboren um 425 (Religion: germ.), Sohn von Angantyr II. von Angeln (siehe 9349).
