2 CONT
2 CONT Ælfflæd of Mercia (II)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Ælfflæd was the daughter of Ceolwulf I of Mercia, and later married Wigmund of Mercia. Their son, Wigstan of Mercia, inherited the throne in 840 but, declining the kingship, appointed his mother as regent. She was deposed from thi
2 CONC s position by Beorhtwulf of Mercia.[1] Ælfflæd should not be confused with her earlier Mercian namesake, Ælfflæd, the daughter of Offa of Mercia.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ Ashley, Mike. The Mammoth Book of British Kings and Queens (1999) ISBN 0786706929
2 CONT
