2 CONT Cynehelm
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopediaJump to: navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Kenelm (or Cynehelm) was an Anglo-Saxon saint, venerated throughout medieval England, and mentioned in the Canterbury Tales (the Nun's Priest's Tale, 290-299). William of Malmesbury, writing in the 12th century, recounted th
2 CONC at "there was no place in England to which more pilgrims travelled than to Winchcombe on Cynehelm's feast day".
2 CONT
2 CONT In legend, St Cynehelm was a member of the royal family of Mercia, a boy king and martyr, murdered by an ambitious relative.
