2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Caradoc Freichfras ap Llyr o Gwynedd was born after 450. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was lord of Gloucester in right of his father, was grandson of Brychan Brecheiniog, prince and lord of Brecknock. Supposedly, he was a contemporary with King Arthur, who lived about the year 400, one of the knights of his Round
2 CONC  Table and lord keeper of "y Castell Dolorus" or the Dolorous Tower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caradog Vreichvras, or Cradoc Fraich Fras, means Cradoc "with the strong arm." He was also called Caradog Fawr. He also went by the name of Caradog "the Elder" (Fawr = the Elder). 
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p94.htm#i11738 )
