1 NAME Tryffin Farfog Brenin Dyfed
2 GIVN Tryffin Farfog
2 NSFX Brenin Dyfed
2 NICK Tryffin ap Owain Fraisg
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 405
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tryffin Farfog (Tryffin the Bearded), King of Dyfed, appears in The Expulsion of the Deisi as descended from Eochaid, the member of the Deisi who went to Wales. This lineage appears also in some Welsh genealogies (
2 CONC see, for instance, Peter Bartrum, below). The Expulsion of the Deisi is now considered fictional, however. Tryffin Farfog is given as the son of Owain Fraisg in other Welsh manuscripts, and in still others he is given as descended
2 CONC  from Magnus Maximus. None of these lineages can be shown to be true. Please do not give him parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father, according to The Expulsion of the Deisi -- https://www.geni.com/people/Aed-Brosc-brenin-Dyfed/6000000007386717300?through=367836847910003955 
2 CONT Bartrum labels this person as also being Owain Fraisg.
2 CONT Magnus Maximus (Maxen Wledig) -- https://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-Maximus-Western-Roman-Emperor/5365308074870051638
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393650888 (February 6, 2023; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT Triffyn Farfog was probably an historical person; the father given to him in the genealogies was legendary, however; his profile can be found here:  [https://www.geni.com/people/Aed-Brosc-The-Expulsion-of-the-Déisi/600000000738671
2 CONC 7300]
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Maxen Wledig and the Welsh Genealogies; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id19.html. (Steven Ferry, February 10, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Rulers of Brycheiniog - The Unanswered Questions; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id161.html. (Steven Ferry, March 16, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Legendary Kingdom of Seisyllwg; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id123.html. (Steven Ferry, September 11, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Harleian Ms 3859; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id129.html. (Steven Ferry, March 8, 2021.)
