2 CONT
2 CONT The above Monarchs of Northumbria link shows that Alhred of Bernicia bc740 was King of Northumbria succeeding Ethelred Moll from 765 to 774 and then was exiled. Alhred of Bernicia was descended from Brynhorn born 720 and his fathe
2 CONC r Bofa b690. This paternal line came from Alric bc543 a son of King Ida of Northumbria. Alhred had a son named Eahlwine b760 who according to Quote from Project Medlands: from Florence of Worcester: Alchred was "filius Eahlwine...
2 CONC qui fuit Alhred...qui fuit Byrnhom, qui fuit Bofa, qui fuit Bleacman, qui fuit Ealric, qui fuit Idæ" (was Missing a generation or two.).  Son of Moll named Ethelred took the throne from 774-779 followed by Aelfwald 779-88 who was 
2 CONC murdered(son of Oswulf). Aelfwald was  father of Osgyfu and Aelfwald II. Osgyfu from the line of Oswulf then married Alchred from the line of Alric to Alhred who was king 765-74. Osgyfu and Alchred then were parents of Alchfleda w
2 CONC ho married the Earl of Bamburgh, Eadwulf and had their son (heir) Ealdred of Bamburgh.
