2 CONT From Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wermund or Garmund is an ancestor of the Mercian royal family through his son Uffe (Offa). Some genealogies present him as a son of Wihtlaeg and a grandson of Odin, but the Danish histories written by Saxo Grammaticus disagree wit
2 CONC h this concept.
2 CONT
2 CONT He appears to have reigned in Angel, and his story is preserved by certain Danish historians, especially Saxo Grammaticus. According to these traditions, his reign was long and happy, though its prosperity was eventually marred by
2 CONC  the raids of a warlike king named Athislus, who slew Frowinus, the governor of Schleswig, in battle. Frowinus's death was avenged by his two sons, Keto and Wigo, but their conduct in fighting together against a single man was tho
2 CONC ught to constitute a national disgrace, which was only reconciled by the subsequent single combat of Offa.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that Athislus, though called king of the Swedes by Saxo, was really identical with the Eadgils, lord of the Myrgingas, mentioned in Widsith. As Eadgils was a contemporary of Ermanaric (also known as Eormenric
2 CONC ), who died about 370, his date would agree with the indication given by the genealogies which place Wermund nine generations above Penda. Frowinus and Wigo are doubtless to be identified with the Freawine and Wig who figure among
2 CONC  the ancestors of the kings of Wessex.
2 CONT
