2 CONT Rhodri ap Hywel (died 953) was a king of Deheubarth in south Wales, and son of Hywel Dda.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Hywel's death in 950 Deheubarth was shared between Rhodri and his two brothers, Edwin and Owain. The sons of Hywel were not able to keep hold of Gwynedd, which was reclaimed for the traditional dynasty of Aberffraw by Iago ap I
2 CONC dwal and Ieuaf ap Idwal, the sons of Idwal Foel.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 952 Iago and Ieuaf invaded the south, penetrating as far as Dyfed. The sons of Hywel retaliated by invading the north in 954, reaching as far north as the Conwy valley before being defeated in a battle at Llanrwst and being obl
2 CONC iged to retreat to Ceredigion.
