1 NOTE Alpín mac Echdach may refer to two persons. The first person is a presumed king of Dál Riata in the late 730s. The second is the father of Kenneth MacAlpin (Cináed mac Ailpín). The name Alpín is taken to be a Pictish one, derived 
2 CONC from the Anglo-Saxon name Ælfwine; Alpín's patronymic means son of Eochaid or son of Eochu.
2 CONT A wiki em português trata ambos como sendo a mesma pessoa, colocando Alpin como descendente de Conall Gabhrain, do velho reino ‘dalriádico’.
