1 NOTE King of the Scots (from 889), son of Constantine I and successor to Eochaid and Giric (reigned 878-889). His reign coincided with renewed invasions by the Danes, who came less to plunder and more to occupy the lands bordering Scot
2 CONC land and the Anglo-Saxon kingdoms. He was also embroiled in efforts to reduce the highland robber tribes. By one account he was slain at Dunnottar, meeting a Danish invasion; by another he died of infirmity brought on by his campa
2 CONC igns against the highlanders. He was succeeded by his cousin Constantine II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded: King of the Scots, 889.
1 NOTE Killed in battle. Ascended to the throne 889.Ancestral File Number:<AFN>9G9M-F2
