2 CONT Ealhswith From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was Æthelred Mucil, Ealdorman of the Gaini. She was married in 868, to Alfred the Great, king of Wessex. The children of Alfred and Ealhswith included Edward the Elder, later king of Wessex, Ælfthryth, who married Baldw
2 CONC in II, Count of Flanders, and Ethelfleda, who ruled as Lady of the Mercians. After Alfred's death in 899, Ealhswith became a nun. She died on 5 December 905, and is buried in St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester, Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ealhswith
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ealhswith (født ca. 852, død 5. desember 905) var gift med kong Alfred den store av England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hun tilhørte gainerne, en folkegruppe fra Mercia. Hennes mor var Eadburga Saxe-Mercia, og faren var Ethelred Mucil, ealdorman for gainerne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ealhswith og Alfred fikk fem eller seks barn, deriblant sønnen Edvard og datteren Ethelfleda av Mercia. Datteren ble dronning av Mercia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Etter Alfreds død i 899 gikk Ealhswith i kloster. Hun døde 5. desember 905, og ble gravlagt i St. Mary's Abbey i Winchester, Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ealhswith (or Ealswitha) of the Gaini was born c. 852 in Mercia. Her name means "Temple strength".
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was Æthelred Mucil, Ealdorman of the Gaini. She was married in 868, to Alfred the Great, king of Wessex. The children of Alfred and Ealhswith included Edward the Elder, later king of Wessex, Ælfthryth, who married Baldw
2 CONC in II, Count of Flanders, and Ethelfleda, who ruled as Lady of the Mercians.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Alfred's death in 899, Ealhswith became a nun. She died on 5 December 905, and is buried in St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester, Hampshire.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT After Alfred's death, she became a nun at St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester around 901.  She died on either 12/5 or 12/8 in 905.  After her death, she was considered a saint by many people.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Became a nun after her husband's death
