2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 852 in Mercia, Consort of Alfred the Great and mother of Edward the Elder.
2 CONT Died Dec 5 905, she was widowed and became a nun.
2 CONT She was a nun in the abbey that she had founded in 903, Nunnaminster (St. Mary's Abbey) in Winchester. However, she was not buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried first in Winchester New Minster, then, when the new abbey church of Hyde was consecrated in 1110, the bodies of Alfred, his wife Ealhswith, and his son Edward the Elder were carried in state through Winchester to be
2 CONC  interred once more before the high altar. Their royal presence made Hyde Abbey a popular pilgrimage destination.
