2 CONC s/MedLands/ Medieval Lands: A prosopography of medieval European noble and royal families], visited May 6, 2018. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/anglosaxonchroni00gile#page/10/mode/2up The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle], trans. J. A. Giles (London, 1914), p.10. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/657/pg657.txt The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle], trans. Rev. James Ingram (London, 1823), with additional readings from the translation of Dr. J. A. Giles (London, 1847).
2 CONT
2 CONT * Anglo-Saxon Bishops, Kings & Nobles, Eng. 104, p. 255.
2 CONT * The Saga Library, F Ice. 1, "Heimskringla", v. 1, p. 16, v. 2, p. 148.
2 CONT * The Viking Age, Gen. Hist. 19, v. 1, p. 28-68.
