1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Roger of Wendover records that "rex Northanhumbrorum Athelredus" fled in 844 and was replaced by "Readwlfus", but that the latter was killed in battle "apud Alutthelia" with "consul Alfredus" whereupon Æthelred was
2 CONC  restored[1116]. Roger of Wendover records that "Athelredo rege Northanhumbrorum" was killed in 848 and succeeded by "Osbertus" who reigned for eighteen years[1117].
2 CONT ___________________
2 CONT This addition to the sons of Eadwulf II d810 comes from Project Medlands/Kings of Northumbria with sources attached. According to the source in Medlands "ANNALES LINDISFARNENSES 797, MGH 58 XIX p. 506" the second wife of Eadwulf I
2 CONC I might have been a daughter of Emperor Charlemagne (filiam regis Karoli) because Eadwulf II fled for protection in 1807-08 to the court of Charlemagne and was granted a papal delegation to return with Eadwulf and his new wife to 
2 CONC Northumbria. With that being done, Eadwulf II was restored to his position as king and he had a son by his new wife named Readwulf  born c808-810. However, Eadwulf's eldest son Eanred succeeded to the throne after 810 and ruled un
2 CONC til his death in 840. Then Eanred's son Aethelred ruled until 844 when he was deposed by the thanes and Readwulf.. By the end of 844 Readwulf  was killed in battle by Aethelred who then ruled again until his death in 848. Osberht 
2 CONC was then named as king in 848 
