2 CONT 1 NAME Edward I, "The Elder" King of /England/
1 NOTE Acceded 899-924.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward 'the Elder'
2 CONT Well-trained by Alfred, his son Edward 'the Elder' (reigned 899-924) wasa bold soldier who defeated the Danes in Northumbria at Tettenhall in 910and was acknowledged by the Viking kingdom of York. The kings ofStrathclyde and the S
2 CONC cots submitted to Edward in 921. By military successand patient planning, Edward spread English influence and control. Muchof this was due to his alliance with his formidable sister Aethelflaed,who was married to the ruler of Merc
2 CONC ia and seems to have governed thatkingdom after her husband's death.
2 CONT Edward was able to establish an administration for the kingdom ofEngland, whilst obtaining the allegiance of Danes, Scots and Britons.Edward died in 924, and he was buried in the New Minster which he had hadcompleted at Winchester
2 CONC . Edward was twice married, but it is possiblethat his eldest son Athelstan was the son of a mistress.
2 CONT [large-G675.FTW]
