1 NOTE From THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry, chart pg 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 50:
2 CONT
2 CONT 15.     Edward the Elder, 875-924; King of England from 901; a cool, efficient leader supported by a growing national spirit, he methodically turned back the Danes in their new attempt to overrun the island, defeated them piecemea
2 CONC l and by the time of his death was not only the supreme English king but the only English king.  He mar. (3) Eadgifu, d. 961, dau. of Sigehelm, Ealdorman of Kent.  He was succeeded by a son Athelstan, who managed to meet the new D
2 CONC anish Outbreaks with suddess.  At the time of his death 939, the realm was at peace.  His only son predeceased him so the crown passed to his brother Edmund.
