2 CONC    Edward was a Bretwala (King of Kings). First King of all England. Ruled from 899-924. K&Q says from 899-925. Several daughters became nuns.
2 CONT    K: Edward I, "The Pious."   Roots: Edward the Elder, Saxon King of England, married (2) Alfflaed, (3) Eadgifu.   Sureties: Edward I, the Elder, King of England 901-924. Born 875 and died 924.
2 CONT    Kirby: Eadweard.   Young: Edward the Elder, died 924, King of England and overlord of the Welsh princes.   Warrior Kings: "Edward, eldest son, was a warrior rather than a scholar, though in this capacity he probably took a good
2 CONC  deal of weight from his father's shoulders. The relationship between father and son seems to have been amicable."
