2 CONT m thirdly (before 867) ---, daughter of CINAED & his wife ---.  The Fragmentary Annals of Ireland record in 867 "an encounter between Oisle son of the king of Norway and Amlaib his brother", adding that "the king had three sons, A
2 CONC mlaib, Imar and Oisle, Oisle was the least of them in age", recounting a lengthy romanticised account of the killing of Asl by his brother Olaf which includes Asl suggesting to Olaf that "if your wife i.e. the daughter of Cinaed d
2 CONC oes not love you, why not give her to me"[1157].  There is no way to judge the accuracy of the information concerning Olaf´s wife.  Clare Downham refers to works which attempt to identify "Cinaed" either as Kenneth I King of Scotl
2 CONC and, as "Cinaed mac Conaing king of Brega, an ally of Olaf who was killed in 851" or "indeed yet another Cinaed", concluding that "either identification is possible, if the lady is not a figure of fiction"[1158]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amla%C3%ADb_Conung
