2 CONC  II planned to change the laws of succession. See ESSH, pp. 512–515.
2 CONT
2 CONT   10. ^ ESSH, p. 516.
2 CONT
2 CONT   11. ^ Annals of the Four Masters, s.a. 998: "Dúngal Cináed's son, was killed by Gille Coemgáin, Cináed's son." It is not clear if the Cináeds (Kenneths) referred to are Cináed mac Maíl Coluim (Kenneth II) or his nephew and names
2 CONC ake Cináed mac Duib (Kenneth III). Smyth, pp. 221–222, makes Dúngal following ESSH p. 580.
2 CONT
