1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Elfelda/Aeflaed was consort to King Edward I 'the Elder'; she is called by one source the daughter of Ealdorman Aethelhelm (although there were several ealdormen of this name at the time, this had been taken to refer to the aaldor
2 CONC man of Wiltshire). She had seven children of whom two daughters would have progeny.
