2 CONT Ælfweard, King of England (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #106615, d. 1 August 924
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=3 Dec 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT      Ælfweard, King of England was the son of Eadweard I, King of Wessex and Ælflæd (?). (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 1 August 924 at Oxford, Oxfordshire, England. (1) He was buried at Winchester Cathedral, Winchester, Hampshire, England. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10662.htm#i106615
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT by wiki
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethelweard was born in Wessex around the year 904. He did not have a long reign. According to one version of the Anglo-Saxon chronicle, Ethelweard was appointed king on 17 July 924 after the death of his father, Edward the Elder. 
2 CONC He died sixteen days later on 2 August 924. Some claim that he was killed on the orders of his half-brother Athelstan, who became the next king. Ethelweard never married. He was buried at Winchester.
