1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Eadgifu was the daughter of Edward I 'the Elder', king of England, and Elfleda. Between 916 and 919 she became the second wife of Charles III 'the Simple', king of France, who in 922 was imprisoned by Heribert II de Vermandois. To
2 CONC  protect the safety of her son Louis, Eadgifu took him to England in 923 to the court of her half-brother Athelstan, king of England. Louis became known as Louis d'Outremer because he was raised in England. He stayed there until 9
2 CONC 36, when he was called back to France to be crowned king. Eadgifu accompanied him. From then she lived in the Abbey of Notre Dame in Laon until, in 951, she married Heribert de Vermandois, Count of Meaux, son of her first husband'
2 CONC s captor. After her death, Heribert became Abbot of St. Médard in Soissons.
