2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT EadgythFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT For other people named Eadgyth, see Eadgyth (disambiguation). A statue in the Cathedral of Magdeburg that is often assumed to represent Otto and Edith Edith of England (Old English: Ēadgȳð) (910 – 26 January 946), also spelt Eadgy
2 CONC th or Ædgyth, was the daughter of Edward the Elder, King of England and Ælfflæd, and the wife of Otto I, Holy Roman Emperor.
2 CONT
