2 CONC ed-great-granddau.... Retrieved 20 January 2010.
2 CONT 2. ^ Satter, Raphael G. (20 Jan 2010). "Discovery News". Bones of early English princess found in Germany. http://news.discovery.com/archaeology/english-princess-bones.html. Retrieved 21 January 2010.
2 CONT 3. ^ German cathedral bones 'are Saxon queen Eadgyth, BBC News, 16 June 2010
2 CONT 4. ^ Remains of first king of England's sister found in German cathedral, The Guardian, 17 June 2010
2 CONT 5. ^ The Times, Simon de Bruxelles, 17 June 2010
2 CONT 6. ^ Bones confirmed as those of Saxon Princess Eadgyth, University of Bristol, 17 June 2010
