2 TITL Edmund I of England - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 NOTE Edmund I "THE Magnificent", born about 922 in Wessex, England; died May 26, 946 at Pucklechurch, Gloucestershire, England; was crowned King of England on October 27, 940; killed at a banquet by an exiled outlaw, LEOFA; buried at G
2 CONC lastonbury, England; married Elgiva, born about 922, in Wessex, England; died 944 in England; after her death she was hallowed as a saint and miracles were worked at her tomb at Shaftesbury, England.
1 NOTE Edmund I the Elder, King of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 921
2 CONT Acceded: 29 NOV 939, Kingston-upon-Thames, Surrey
2 CONT Died: 26 MAY 946, Pucklechurch, Dorset
2 CONT Interred: Glastonbury Abbey, Somerset
2 CONT Notes:
2 CONT Reigned 940-946
2 CONT Murdered: An Outlaw, Leolf, stabbed him to death at a banquet toSt.Augustine
2 CONT He expelled the Norse King Olaf from Northumbria in 944. He supported
2 CONT Dunstan in the reintroduction of the Monastic rule of St. Benedict.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: , Edward the Elder, King of England, b. 869
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: , Eadgifu (Edgiva), b. BEF 905
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to , AElfgifu (St.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Child 1: , Edwy (EAdwig) the Fair, King of England, b. CIR 942
2 CONT Child 2: , Daughter
2 CONT Child 3: , Edgar the Peaceful, King of England, b. 944
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to , AEthelflaed of Domerham
2 CONT
