1 NOTE Edmund I "THE Magnificent", born about 922 in Wessex, England; died May 26, 946 at Pucklechurch, Gloucestershire, England; was crowned King of England on October 27, 940; killed at a banquet by an exiled outlaw, LEOFA; buried at G
2 CONC lastonbury, England; married Elgiva, born about 922, in Wessex, England; died 944 in England; after her death she was hallowed as a saint and miracles were worked at her tomb at Shaftesbury, England.
1 NOTE Data From Lynn Jeffrey Bernhard, 2445 W 450 South #4, Springville UT  84663-4950 
2 CONT email - bernhardengineer@netscape.net
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: King of England 93946. The son of Edward the Elder, he succeeded his half-brother, Athelstan, as king in 939. He succeeded in regaining control of Mercia, which on his accession had fallen to the Norse inhabitants of N
2 CONC orthumbria, and of the Five Boroughs, an independent confederation within the Danelaw. He then moved on to subdue the Norsemen in Cumbria and finally extended his rule as far as southern Scotland. As well as uniting England, he bo
2 CONC lstered his authority by allowing St Dunstan to reform the Benedictine order. He was killed in 946 at Pucklechurch, Gloucestershire, by an outlawed robber.
2 CONT
2 CONT  -- http://www.begent.net/history
