1 NOTE Edmund I (921-46), Saxon king of the English (939-46), the son of KingEdward the Elder. He participated in the Battle of Brunanburh in 937and succeeded his half brother Athelstan as king in 939. The followingyear Olaf Godfreyson, 
2 CONC a Viking ruler of Dublin, seized the territoryof Northumbria in northern England and extended his rule as far southas Leicester. After Olaf's death in 941, Edmund made war on theVikings, expelling them from the country three years
2 CONC  later. In 945Edmund occupied the kingdom of Strathclyde, west of Northumbria, andturned it over to his ally Malcolm I MacDonald, king of Scotland(reigned 943-54). The following year Edmund was stabbed to death by arobber and was 
2 CONC succeeded by his brother Edred (reigned 945-55). Edmundwas known as a legal reformer, especially for his restrictions on theblood feud.
