1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Son of Baudouin I, count of Flanders, and Judith, daughter of Emperor Charles 'the Bald', Baudouin was born about 863, and became count of Flanders on his father's death in 879. From his stronghold at Bruges he maintained, as his 
2 CONC father Baudouin I before him, a vigorous defence of his lands against the incursions of the Norsemen. On his mother's side a descendant of Charlemagne, he strengthened the dynastic importance of his family by marrying Elftrudis/Al
2 CONC fthryth of Wessex, daughter of Alfred 'the Great', king of England. Baudouin II and Elftrudis had four children, of whom their son Arnulf I would continue his line. He annexed lands and rights in the area between the river Schelde
2 CONC  and Artois and had his opponents murdered. He died on 10 September 918 and was buried in the Abbey of St.Peter in Ghent.
1 NOTE Boudewijn II de Kale, geb. omstr. 864, graaf van Vlaanderen 879-918, usurpeerde na afloop van invallen van de Noormannen van de jaren 879-883 grondbezit en rechten in de hele streek tussen Schelde enArtois, gold als grondlegger va
2 CONC n Vlaanderen als terrotoriaal vorstendom, wisselde herhaaldelijk van partij in de strijd tussen de diverse Westfrankische Koningen en liet aartsbisschop Fulco van Reims(900) en graaf Heribert I van Vermandois (voor 907) vermoorden
2 CONC , richtte een groot aantal burchten op ter bescherming van zijn gebied, overl. 10 sept. 918, begr. Gent, tr. omstr. 884 Aelfthryth van Wessex, geb. omstr. 872 (dochter van Alfred I de Grote, koning van Engeland 871-899, en Elswith
2 CONC a van Gainsborough), stak omstr. 884 het Kanaal over, gravin van Vlaanderen, overl. 7 juni 929
