2 CONC  “the daughter of Malcolm King of Scots” (whose succession is recorded in 1005)[862].  Snorre records the marriage of "Sigurd the Thick" and "a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm"[863].  It appears unlikely that Sigurd´s wife c
2 CONC ould have been King Malcolm´s daughter Donada (as shown in many secondary sources, including the Complete Peerage[864]) if it is correct that Donada´s recorded husband Findlaech was killed in 1020 and that their son was born in [1
