2 CONT
2 CONT Cináed mac Duib (Modern Gaelic: Coinneach mac Dhuibh)[1] anglicised as Kenneth III, and nicknamed An Donn, "the Chief" or "the Brown",[2] (before 967–25 March 1005) was King of Scots from 997 to 1005. He was the son of Dub (Dub ma
2 CONC c Maíl Coluim). Many of the Scots sources refer to him as Giric son of Kenneth son of Dub, which is taken to be an error.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT The only event reported in Kenneth's reign is the killing of Dúngal mac Cináeda by Gille Coemgáin mac Cináeda, by the Annals of the Four Masters s.a. 999. It is not certain that this refers to events in Scotland, and whether one o
2 CONC r both were sons of this Kenneth, or of Kenneth II of Scotland, or some other person or persons, is not known.[4] Kenneth was killed in battle at Monzievaird in Strathearn by Malcolm II (Máel Coluim mac Cináeda) in 1005.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Whether Boite mac Cináeda was a son of this Kenneth, or of Kenneth II, is uncertain, although most propose this Kenneth. A son, or grandson of Boite, was reported to be killed by Malcolm II in 1032 in the Annals of Ulster.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth's granddaughter, Gruoch daughter of Boite (Gruoch ingen Boite meic Cináeda) — Shakespeare's Lady Macbeth — was wife firstly of Gille Coemgáin, Mormaer of Moray, and secondly of King Macbeth; her son by Gille Coemgáin, Lula
2 CONC ch (Lulach mac Gille Coemgáin), would briefly succeed Macbeth as King of Scotland. The meic Uilleim, descendants of William fitz Duncan by his first marriage, were probably descended from Kenneth.[7]
1 NOTE "ALPIN"; KING OF SCOTLAND 997-1005; KILLED AT MONZIEVAIRD BY MALCOLM II
1 NOTE Murdered by Malcolm II, King of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth III of Scotland
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth III (Cináed mac Duib) was King of Scots from 997 to 1005. He wasthe son of King Dubh, fourth cousin of the previous king Constantine III,and first cousin of his successor Malcolm II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth was the last king of Scotland to succeed to the throne throughthe system of tanistry, whereby the succession was shared between twofamily lines and the dying king named the person from the other familyline who was to succe
2 CONC ed him. The system was much discredited as itensured that the two royal families of the Kingdom of Scotland were in aconstant state of war with each other.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth and his son Giric were both killed in the Battle of Monzievaird,Tayside on March 25, 1005. It was his first cousin Malcolm, succeedinghim at the battle, who abolished the tanistry system by killing all ofKenneth's male des
2 CONC cendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Kenneth had a granddaughter, Gruoch, via his son Bodhe. Gruoch'sfirst husband was Gillacomgain, Mormaer of Moray. They had a son calledLulach. She then married King Macbeth of Scotland (becoming LadyMacbeth). On the death
2 CONC  of Macbeth, her son via her first marriage(Kenneth III's great-grandson), succeeded to the throne, becoming KingLulach of Scotland.
1 NOTE He ruled from 997 to 1005.
1 NOTE He ruled from 997 to 1005.
