2 CONT Malcolm II of Alba, King of Scotland was born circa 954.1 He was the son of Kenneth II of Alba, King of Scotland. He married an unknown person circa 980.2 He died on 25 November 1034 at Glamis Castle, Glamis, Angus, Scotland, kill
2 CONC ed by his kinsmen.3 He was buried at Isle of Iona, Argyllshire, Scotland.3
2 CONT      Malcolm II of Alba, King of Scotland succeeded to the title of King Malcolm of Strathclyde between 990 and 991.1 He was deposed as King of Strathclyde in 995.1 He gained the title of King Malcolm of Strathclyde in 997.1 He su
2 CONC cceeded to the title of King Malcolm II of Scotland on 25 March 1005.1 He gained the title of King Malcolm of Lothian circa 1016.1 He gained the title of King Malcolm of Alba. He gained the title of Prince Malcolm of Cumbria.1
