1 NOTE From THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry,  chart pg 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 44:
2 CONT
2 CONT 19.     Malcolm II MacKenneth, murdered 25 Nov. 1034; King of Scots from 25 March 1005.  In 1008 at Carham, Northumbria, with the help of Uchtred, Earl of Northumbria, won the rich wheatlands of Bernicia from King Canute, uniting 
2 CONC the four Kingdoms into the geographical Scotland of today; overcame the Danes 1017; published a code of laws 1018; succeeded in having his grandson Duncan appointed King of Strathclyde and Cumbria.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amie, Adam and FAL
1 NOTE 1  UID 7F37D85FF3FAC54AA5D4844E303A02E68624
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Scots 1005-1034
2 CONT Was murderd
2 CONT
2 CONT 1  UID C4755771C14103498626D3CBD0F047EA8ACB
1 NOTE REFN: 1317[FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT    King of Scotland from 1005 to 1034, the first to reign over an extentof land roughly corresponding to much of modern Scotland.
2 CONT    Malcolm succeeded to the throne after killing his predecessor, KennethIII, and allegedly secured his territory by defeating a Northumbrian armyat the battle of Carham (c. 1016); he not only
2 CONT confirmed the Scottish hold over the land between the rivers Forth andTweed but also secured Strathclyde about the same time. Eager to securethe royal succession for his daughter's son Duncan, he tried to eliminatepossible rival c
2 CONC laimants; but Macbeth, with royal connections to bothKenneth II and Kenneth III, survived to challenge the succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT To cite this page: "Malcolm II" Encyclopædia Britannica
2 CONT <http://www.britannica.com/eb/article?eu=51525&tocid=0&query=malcolm%20ii>
2 CONT King of Alba and Strathcllyde. Conquered Lothian in 1018, Said to havemarried an Irish woman from Ossory. Killed by kinsman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reigned from 1005-1034.
