1 NOTE Malcolm II of Alba, King of Scotland succeeded to the title of King Malcolm of Strathclyde between 990 and 991. he was deposed as King od Strathclyde in 995. He succeeded to the title of King Malcolm of Scotland on 25/3/1005. he g
2 CONC ained the title of King Malcolm of Lothian c 1016. He gained the title of King Malcolm of Alba. He gained the title of Prince Malcolm of Cumbria.He was killed by his kinsmen. He was buried in Isle of Iona, Agryllshire, Scotland.
