2 CONC , Cerdic and Cynric, his son, with 5 ships....519. This year Cerdic and Cynric undertook the government of the West Saxons; the same year they fought with the Britons at a place called Charford. From that day have reigned the chil
2 CONC dren of the West Saxon kings. 530. They conquered the isle of Wight...534. This year died Cerdic, the first king of the West Saxons. Cynric his son succeeded to the government, and reigned afterwards 26 winters." (ASC, text by Ing
2 CONC ram, Everyman's edition. See the following dates: 495, 519, 530, 854; CCN 230). (See Trelawney Dayrell Reed, The Rise of Wessex, chart p. 31, gens. 1-8. This also discusses Cerdic's parentage.   RC: Cerdic, of ancient Saxony, King
2 CONC  of the West Saxons, 519-534. Invaded Hampshire in 496.
