2 CONC he fatherof Cynric and son of Cerdic, so it is accepted as such for this compilation.
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT King in Wessex; Came to Britain with his son Cynric and "fem skip" in 495.
2 CONT Landed in Britain in 495 and in six years subdued the natives in what later
2 CONT became the Kingdom of the West Saxons, or Wessex. First King of the West
2 CONT Saxons in 519.
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT AS Kr”nike; http://home.att.net/~a.junkins/anglo1.html#X2097152
1 NOTE Cerdic, King of Wessex
2 CONT Died in 534
2 CONT
2 CONT Cerdic, a patriarch of royalty in Saxony, landed in Hampshire in 495 andin 519 gained a victory at Charford. He was first crowned King of theWest Saxons, when, as it is reported, the legendary King Arthur, who hadhis castle on the
2 CONC  steep coast of Cornwall, yielded to him the section ofland now known as Hampshire and Somerset. In 520, being unable to extendhis rule west of the Avon and defeated at Badbury, co. Dorset, Cedricwithdrew. Ten years later he conqu
2 CONC ered the Isle of Wight. He died in 534.Cerdic is said to be the founding figure of the West Saxon dynasty.However, much of this is obscure and not documented, subject to disputeby history scholars. There was no secure chronicle in
2 CONC  the 6th century.(Wurts)
2 CONT
2 CONT Another view:
2 CONT Cerdic and his son Cynric landed in the area of Southhampton in 495 A.D.,and then moved north into what is now Hampshire and Wiltshire to foundThe Kingdom of the West Saxons or Wessex. Cerdic met great resistancefrom the last of t
2 CONC he Romano-Britons under a shadowy leader who lays asgood a claim as any to having been the "real" King Arthur. Cerdic wascrowned as the 1st King of West Saxons at Winchester 532, although somesay he reigned from 519 on. The times 
2 CONC were very chaotic, and althoughleaders such as Cerdic are historical figures, much of the actual historyis shrouded in legend.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cerdic had the following sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynric
2 CONT Creoda (Not all records show Creoda, and those that do suggest he wasCynric's father. It is more likely that Cynric and Creoda are the sameperson.)
2 CONT
2 CONT AKA 1st King of the West Saxons. Crowned at Winchester in 532. Some sayhe ascended in 519, others 534.
2 CONT
2 CONT For ancestors of Cerdic, the Anglo Saxon Chronicles attempts to linkBedwig to the Biblical Noah, while the Prose Edda shows further descentfrom Thor and then attempts to link to Greek mythology.
2 CONT
2 CONT REF: Royal Genealogies DB: "The genealogy prior to Cerdic should beconsidered a reignal one & not one of blood, as this always borders onlegend."
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE King of the West Saxons 519-534.  He was a Saxon Ealdorman who founded asettlement on the coast of Hampshire in 495.  He assumed the title "Kingof the West Saxons" in 519 and became the ancestor of the English RoyalLine.
