2 CONC he fatherof Cynric and son of Cerdic, so it is accepted as such for this compilation.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT A Saxon ealdorman, Cerdic came to England with his son Cynric in 495 and founded a settlement on the coast of Hampshire. In 519 father and son fought the Britons at Charford, and from that year on Cerdic assumed the title of King 
2 CONC of the West Saxons. He and his son conquered the Isle of Wight in about 534, the year that Cerdic died.
1 NOTE He invaded Hampshire in 496. In 487 he led West-Saxons from northern Germany to Britain. He ruled Wessex from 519 to 534 when he either abdicated or died.
