2 CONC  year Cuthwine and Ceawlin fought witht he Britons and slew three kings...and took from them three cities, Gloucester, Cirencester, and Bath." (ASC 577, 854).   RC: Cuthwine, Under-ruler of Wessex. Slain, Battle of Barbery Hill.
