1 OCCU Comte d'Omois (927-993), COUNT
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''CURATOR NOTE''': Son of Heribert II Comte de Vermandois and Adela Capet de Neustria (de France). NOT THE SAME AS Heribert III Comte de Vermandois (who was son of Adalbert & Gerberge). PLEASE DO NOT MERGE THEM TO
2 CONC GETHER.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#Heribertdied980984 Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Northern France] (covering his birth family):
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''HERIBERT [III] "le Vieux"'''  ([910/26]-[983/early 985], bur Lagny)=  
2 CONT
2 CONT * son of '''Heribert II''' and his wife '''Adela Capet de Neustria (France)'''
2 CONT * Flodoard names "Heriberti Adalberti fratris" when recording his marriage, and in a later passage "nepotes Hugonis, Heribertus et Rotbertus"[1306].   
2 CONT * his date of birth has been estimated at [910/15] by Werner[1307], whereas Settipani supports a later estimate of [925/26][1308].  The former appears more consistent with Héribert's participation in his father's war from 938.  If
2 CONC  the latter is correct, comte Héribert would have been more than 20 years younger than his wife, which seems unlikely.  There appears to be no basis for deciding between one or the other.   
2 CONT * He is documented with his father between 938 and 942 in the latter's war against King Louis IV, submitting to the king with his father in 942.   
2 CONT * Under the division of territories organised after his father's death in 943, Héribert became '''Comte d'Omois''' and received the fortress of Château-Thierry as well as the abbey of Saint-Médard, Soissons.   
2 CONT * King Lothaire appointed him comte du palais (comte palatin).   
2 CONT * He succeeded his brother Robert in 967 as''' Comte de Meaux et de Troyes.'''   
2 CONT * His proposed death date range in [983/early 985] is estimated on the following basis.  A letter of Gerbert dated 983 records that "Heriberti Trecassini et Oddonis comitis filii Tedbaldi" were enemies of "Adelbero Remonis archiep
2 CONC iscopus"[1309].  However, a letter dated to Apr 985 names "Ottonis et Heriberti", while a letter dated to mid-985 records that "Ottonem, Heribertum" made peace with the archbishop[1310].  Another letter of Gerbert dated to [late 9
2 CONC 86/early 987] records that "O et Heribertus comites" were part of the council of Emma Queen of France[1311].  It is assumed that "Oddonis/Ottonem/O" all refer to the same person.  However, it is suggested that only the first lette
2 CONC r applies to Héribert [III], the change to Héribert [V] (nephew and successor of Héribert [III], son of the latter's brother Robert) being indicated in the subsequent letters by "Heribertum" being named after "Ottonem" instead of 
2 CONC before, which suggests that he was the junior of the two from Apr 985.   
2 CONT * The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records the burial of "comes Trecensis Heribertus II cognomento Vetulus" in "abbatiam Latiniaci"[1312].     
2 CONT * m (951) as her second husband, EADGIFU, widow of CHARLES III "le Simple" King of the Franks, daughter of EDWARD I King of Wessex & his second wife Ælfleda --- ([902/05][1313]-26 Sep after 951, bur Abbaye de Saint-Médard de Soiss
2 CONC ons).   
2 CONT * Flodoard names "Ottogeba regina, mater Ludowici regis" when recording her second marriage[1314]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on England Anglo-Saxon Danish Kings (covering his wife - he apparently had no children): http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLAND,%20AngloSaxon%20&%20Danish%20Kings.htm#Eadgifudiedaft
2 CONC er951
2 CONT
2 CONT EADWEARD, son of ALFRED King of Wessex & his wife Ealhswith ([872]-Farndon-on-Dee near Chester 17 Jul 924, bur Winchester Cathedral[1622]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([892/94]) ECGWYNN, daughter of --- (-[901/02]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (901 or before) ÆLFLÆD, daughter of ealdorman ÆTHELHELM & his wife Ælswitha --- (-920, bur Winchester Cathedral[1635]).  "Elffled coniux regis" subscribed a 901 charter of King Edward[1636].  The Book of Hyde names "Elf
2 CONC elmi comitis filia Elfleda" as first wife of King Eadweard[1637].  Roger of Wendover calls her "secunda regina sua…Alfleda, Elfelmi comitis filia"[1638]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m thirdly (920) EADGIFU, daughter of SIGEHELM Lord of Meopham, Cooling and Lenham in Kent & his wife --- (-26 Aug 968, bur Canterbury Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Edward "the Elder" & his second wife had [eight] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. EADGIFU ([902/05]-26 Sep after 951, bur Abbaye de Saint-Médard de Soissons).  
2 CONT
2 CONT William of Malmesbury names (in order) "Edfleda, Edgiva, Ethelhilda, Ethilda, Edgitha, Elfgiva" as the six daughters of King Eadweard & his wife "Elfleda", specifying that Edgiva married "king Charles"[1662].  The Book of Hyde nam
2 CONC es "Edgivam" as second of the six daughters of King Eadweard by his first wife "Elfelmi comitis filia Elfleda", specifying that she married "Karolo regi Francorum filio Lodowyci"[1663].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Her birth date range is estimated from the birth of Eadgifu's son in [920/21].  If this is correct, Eadgifu must have been one of King Edward's oldest children by his second marriage.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She fled with her two-year-old son to England in 923 after her first husband was deposed.  She returned to France in 936.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Abbess of Notre Dame de Laon, resigned 951.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Flodoard names "Ottogeba regina, mater Ludowici regis" when recording her second marriage[1664].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([917/19]) as his second wife, CHARLES III "le Simple" King of the Franks, son of LOUIS II "le Bègue" King of the West Franks & his second wife Adélaïde [d'Angoulême]  (posthumously 17 Sep 879-Péronne 7 Oct 929, bur Péro
2 CONC nne St Fursy).  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (951) HERIBERT Comte "le Vieux" [de Vermandois], son of HERIBERT [II] Comte de Vermandois [Carolingian] & his wife Adela de Paris [Capet] ([910/15]-[980/984]).  He succeeded his brother Robert in 967 as Comte de Meaux e
2 CONC t de Troyes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT
2 CONT [1662] William of Malmesbury 126, p. 110.  [1663] Liber Monasterii de Hyda XIV.4, p. 112.  [1664] Flodoard 951, MGH SS III, p. 401. 
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Heribert III, Comte d'Omois: http://thepeerage.com/p36113.htm#i361126
2 CONT
2 CONT Heribert III, Comte d'Omois ▼1 M, #361126, b. 927, d. between 980 and 984 Last Edited=30 May 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Heribert III, Comte d'Omois was born in 927. ▼1 He was the son of Heribert II, Comte de Vermandois and Liégarde de France. ▼1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 980 and 984. ▼1
2 CONT
2 CONT Heribert III, Comte d'Omois gained the title of Comte d'Omois. ▼1
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
