2 CONT
2 CONT Edgar's reign was a peaceful one and the Kingdom of England was at its height.  Edgar consolidated the political unity achieved by his predecessors.  By the end of Edgar's reign, England was sufficiently unified that it was unlike
2 CONC ly to regress back to a state of division among rival kingships.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Edgar's death to the Norman Conquest, there was not a single succession to the throne that was not contested.  Some see Edgar's death as the beginning of the end of Anglo-Saxon England.
