2 CONC  nobles held Edgar to be king north of the Thames, and Edgar aspired to succeed to the English throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Government
2 CONT
2 CONT Though Edgar was not a particularly peaceable man, his reign was a peaceful one. The Kingdom of England was at its height. Edgar consolidated the political unity achieved by his predecessors. By the end of Edgar's reign, England w
2 CONC as sufficiently unified that it was unlikely to regress back to a state of division among rival kingships, as it had to an extent under Eadred's reign.
