1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Curator (dvb) Note: per https://www.berghapedia.nl/index.php?title=Liutgard_van_Vlaanderen According to the necrology of the Blandinien monastery near Ghent, Liutgard died on III Kal Oct. ' (September 29) 961 and w
2 CONC as buried there. In Elten 's Necrologium she is featured on Id. Oct. (October 15), stated, but without year: MEDLANDS has the commonly used death date and no citation for the 935 birth date.  Cawley has the marriage date after 10 
2 CONC July 953 while Pattou has it c. 950.  After 953 would make her 18 if born 935, easily able to have children.  If born 927 then she would be 26 unusually “old” in medieval Europe to have a first child.  But the link above shows the
2 CONC  first child Adele born 950, so we need some fine tuning here but excellent summary by Ben.
2 CONT
2 CONT 927 is a better birth year estimation than 935.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel's summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships:
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *Father: Arnoul de Flandre (885/890 - 964), Comte de Flandre (918-964)
2 CONT *Mother: Adela de Vermandois (915-960)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings:
2 CONT *1. Hildegard (c933-990) wife of Dirk II, Graaf von Holland
2 CONT *3. Baudoin de Flandres (935/940 - 962), husband of Mechtild (Mathilda) von Sachsen 
2 CONT *4. Egbert de Flandre (d. 953)
2 CONT *5. Elstrude de Flandre (d. c966), wife of Siegfried, Comte de Guines
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *Wichmann V (c930-979), Graaf von Hamaland (938-979)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *1. Liutgard (d. 997)
2 CONT *2. Adela (955/960 - 1014/1016), m. firstly Immed Graaf in Utrecht (d. 983), m. secondly Baldric Graaf von Denthe (d. 1021)
2 CONT
2 CONT Basic information and justifications:
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Liutgard de Flandre - backed by FMG, her Dutch Wikipedia page (an English page doesn't exist), both Dutch and German Wikipedia pages for her husband (again, no English page exists), and the English Wikipedia page for her fat
2 CONC her. The family name of "van Vlaanderen" is of course in Dutch, and "von Vlandern" is in German, just as "of Flanders" is the English variant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: c. 935 (backed by FMG and Dutch Wikipedia) - Gent/Gand/Ghent is presumed to be her birth place, though this is not backed by any reliable source that I've seen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Before 18 October, in 962 (Dutch Wikipedia specified 29 September 964, but without providing anything to back it) - Presumed to be in Hamaland, which has a capital of Zutphen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial and Baptism: No reliable information.
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Gravin von Hamaland (Countess of Hamaland), by marriage. The English Wikipedia page says that she married Wichmann, Count of Ghent, which may be part of the confusion regarding her occupation. The English page provides
2 CONC  no sources to back this assertion, whereas FMG relies on primary sources for its assertion of who she married. There should be no question on which is the more accurate, with regard to "Gand" vs. "Hamaland".
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate names: I found one variation of Lietgard, and a mis-spelling of Luitgard (English Wikipedia). I haven't seen a reliable source showing her name as Ledgarde.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liutgard_van_Vlaanderen Liutgard van Vlaanderen in Wikipedia NL]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Flanders (covering her birth family):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS,%20HAINAUT.htm#Liutgarddied962
2 CONT
2 CONT ARNOUL de Flandre, son of BAUDOUIN II "le Chauve" Count of Flanders & his wife Ælfthryth of Wessex ([885/890]-murdered 27 Mar 964, bur Gent, St Pieter).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Arnulfi Comitis names (in order) "Arnulfum, fratrem eius Adelulfum" as the two sons of "Balduinus"[100].  "Arnulfus" is named as son of Count Baudouin II in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin, which specifies that he 
2 CONC succeeded his father in 918 as ARNOUL I "le Grand" Count of Flanders[101].  "Elstrudis comitissa…cum filiis suis Arnulfo et Adelolfo" donated "hereditatem suam Liefsham…in terra Anglorum in Cantia" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for the
2 CONC  soul of "senioris sui Baldwini", by charter dated 11 Sep 918[102].  
2 CONT *Count Arnoul I was responsible for a major expansion of Flemish territory to the south.  He and his brother joined the expedition of Raoul King of the Franks against the Normans in 925 and captured Eu.  Count Arnoul inflicted a h
2 CONC eavy defeat on the Normans in 926.  In 932, he seized the abbey of St Vaast, as well as Douai in Ostrevant.  
2 CONT *In 933, after his brother's death, he seized Boulonnais and Ternois and disinherited his nephews.  Count Arnoul made an alliance with Héribert II Comte de Vermandois in 934, which was sealed by his marriage to the latter's daught
2 CONC er[103].  
2 CONT *Responding to raids by Guillaume Comte [de Normandie], Count Arnoul invaded Ponthieu and in 939 captured Montreuil from Herluin Comte de Ponthieu, although the county was later recaptured by Comte Guillaume's forces.  
2 CONT *"Arnulfus…regis…marchysus" restored property to Saint-Pierre de Gand by charter dated 8 Jul 941, signed by "…Baldwini filii Arnulfi marchysi, Isaac comitis, Arnulfi filii eius, Theoderici comitis, Wenemari advocati…"[104].  
2 CONT *After agreeing to meet Count Guillaume in 942 in order to settle the dispute over Montreuil, Guillaume was murdered, presumably at Count Arnoul's instigation[105].  Count Arnoul was secure in his possession of Montreuil by 949[10
2 CONC 6].  
2 CONT *"Arnulfus Flandrie comes et marchisus" granted use of property "Snellenghem in pago Flandrensi" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for "uxore mea…Adala atque…filio meo Balduino et filia mea Lietgardis" and for deceased "Balduino genitore m
2 CONC eo et Elstrudis genetrice mea atque Heeberto filio meo", and returned "in pago Hainau super fluvio Savo villam…Dulciaca", by charter dated 10 Jul 953[107].  
2 CONT *After the death of his son in 962, Count Arnoul was obliged to cede Artois, Ostrevant, Ponthieu and Amiens to Lothaire King of the West Franks in order to ensure the latter's support for the succession of Count Arnoul's infant gr
2 CONC andson to the county of Flanders[108].  
2 CONT *"Arnulfus marchysus" donated property to Saint-Pierre de Gand by charter dated 5 May 962, signed by "…Baldwini advocati, Theoderici comitis…"[109].  "Arnulfus…comes" donated "villam Canlin" to Saint-Pierre de Gand by charter date
2 CONC d 17 Jun 962, signed by "…Balduini advocati…"[110].  
2 CONT *An undated charter, dated to [962], records the last wishes of "marchysi Arnulfi", noting that "pater meus et mater mea" were buried in the abbey of Saint-Pierre de Gand[111].  
2 CONT *Comte Arnoul was allegedly murdered by Heluin in revenge for the murder of Guillaume I Comte [de Normandie].  The Annales Blandinienses record the death "VI Kal Apr 964" of "Magnus Arnulfus, restaurator huius Blandiniensis coenob
2 CONC ii"[112].  A charter dated 2 Jul 964 records the donation by "bone memorie Arnulfus marchysus" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, signed by "Odgaudi qui susceptor traditionis fuit…Ingelberti advocati…"[113]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [m firstly ---.  
2 CONT *Both Rösch[114] and Europäische Stammtafeln[115] state that Count Arnoul had another wife before marrying Adela de Vermandois.  No evidence has been found concerning this supposed first marriage.  However, as discussed below, the
2 CONC  estimated birth date of Arnoul´s supposed daughter Hildegard, as well as his own advanced age when he married Adela de Vermandois, both suggest an earlier marriage.  
2 CONT *Although logic points to such a first marriage, doubt remains.  The genealogical traces of this family are well marked in numerous contemporary sources.  It is difficult to imagine that all of such sources would have ignored an e
2 CONC arlier marriage of Comte Arnoul, who was such a prominent figure in his day.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT m [secondly] (934) ADELA de Vermandois, daughter of HERIBERT [II] Comte de Vermandois [Carolingian] & his wife Adela [Capet] ([915]-[Bruges 10 Oct] 960, bur Gent, St Pieter).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Arnulfi Comitis names "Adelam, domni Heriberti comitis filiam" as wife of "comes Arnulfus", specifying that she was "duorum Francorum regum, Odonis atque Rotberti, neptem"[116].  "Adala coniunx Arnulfi" is named i
2 CONC n the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin[117].  The Annales Elnonenses Minores records the marriage [undated between 931 and 949] of "Arnulfus" and "Adelam, filiam Heriberti Vermandorum comitis"[118].  
2 CONT *Her marriage was arranged to seal the alliance made in 934 between her father and her future husband[119].  "Arnulfus Flandrie comes et marchisus" granted use of property "Snellenghem in pago Flandrensi" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, 
2 CONC for "uxore mea…Adala atque…filio meo Balduino et filia mea Lietgardis" and for deceased "Balduino genitore meo et Elstrudis genetrice mea atque Heeberto filio meo", by charter dated 10 Jul 953[120].  "Adhela comitissa" freed two s
2 CONC erfs and granted them to the abbey of Saint-Pierre de Gand, for the soul of "fidelis nostri Amalrici", by charter dated 8 Sep 954, signed by "Balduini comitis…Odacri advocati"[121].  
2 CONT *The Annales Blandinienses record the death in 960 of "Adala comitissa"[122]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Arnoul I & his [first] wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  [HILDEGARD ([before 933]-10 Apr 990, bur Egmond).  
2 CONT *The Annales Egmundani name "Hildegardis comitissa" as wife of "Theodericus comes secundus [Hollandensium]" but do not give her origin[123].  The wife of Count Dirk II was the daughter of Count Arnoul according to Rösch, but the a
2 CONC uthor cites no primary source in support of this assertion[124].  Hildegard's naming her two sons Arnulf and Egbert suggests that the affiliation may be correct.  
2 CONT *According to Europäische Stammtafeln[125], Hildegard was the daughter of Count Arnoul by Adela de Vermandois and was born in [934].  This appears difficult to sustain chronologically if Hildegard's first son was born in [950], al
2 CONC though it is not impossible.  
2 CONT *Assuming that her sister Liutgard was born in 935, there is little time for the birth of an earlier daughter after Count Arnoul's marriage in 934, assuming also that the latter date is correct.  This suggests that, if Hildegard w
2 CONC as the daughter of Count Arnoul, she was born from an earlier otherwise unrecorded marriage.  An alternative parentage is suggested by the Chronologia Johannes de Beke which records that Count Dirk II married "Hildegardim (ut cred
2 CONC itor) filiam Ludovici regis Francie"[126].  This is chronologically impossible, assuming that the birth date of Arnoul Count of Holland is correctly estimated as shown in the document HOLLAND.  Hildegard daughter of Louis III King
2 CONC  of France would have been too old for the marriage and any daughter of Louis IV King of France would have been too young.  It is also unlikely that the wife of Count Dirk II was a daughter of Charles III "le Simple" King of Franc
2 CONC e, the birth dates of whose daughters are estimated to [908/16].  There therefore seems no possibility that the Chronologia could even be partially correct in assigning this possible Carolingian French origin to Dirk's wife, altho
2 CONC ugh it is curious how this origin came to be included in the source.  
2 CONT *"Theodericus comes et uxor sua Hildegardis" are named in a charter dated Oct [967/79][127].  "Theoderici et Hildegardis" subscribed a charter dated 30 Sep 975, before "Arnulfi filii eorum [Theoderici et Hildegardis]"[128].  
2 CONT *The Chronologia Johannes de Beke records the death "III Id Apr" of "Hildegardis…sua conthoralis" and her burial at Egmond monastery[129].  The Chronologia Johannes de Beke records the death "III Id Apr" of "Hildegardis…sua contho
2 CONC ralis" and her burial at Egmond monastery[130].  Beke's Egmondsch Necrologium records the death "IV Id Apr" of "Hildegardis uxor [Theoderici 2 comitis] filia Ludovici regis Francie"[131].  Europäische Stammtafeln shows 990 as Hild
2 CONC egarde´s year of death[132], but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT *m ([945/50]) DIRK II Count of Holland, son of DIRK I Count of Holland & his wife Geva --- ([930]-Egmond 6 May 988, bur Egmond).] 
2 CONT *Count Arnoul I & his [second] wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  LIUTGARD de Flandre ([935]-962, before 18 Oct).  
2 CONT *Boer and Cordfunke refer to a 938 meeting, between Count Dirk I, Count Meginhard of Hamaland, and Count Arnulf I of Flanders and his wife Adela, to arrange the betrothals of Hildegard of Flanders and Count Dirk II (son of Count D
2 CONC irk I), and of her sister Liutgard and Wichmann of Hamaland (son of Count Meginhard)[133].  The meeting is alleged to be recorded in the Verbrüderungsbuch der Abtei Reichenau, but no trace of this has been found in the copy consul
2 CONC ted[134].  
2 CONT *"Arnulfus Flandrie comes et marchisus" granted use of property "Snellenghem in pago Flandrensi" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for "uxore mea…Adala atque…filio meo Balduino et filia mea Lietgardis" and for deceased "Balduino genitore m
2 CONC eo et Elstrudis genetrice mea atque Heeberto filio meo", by charter dated 10 Jul 953[135].  This document suggests that Liutgard was not married at the time.  
2 CONT *"Wicmannus…comes" donated "mei juris villam Thesla" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for the soul of "coniugis mee defuncte Lietgardis", by charter dated 18 Oct 962, signed by "comitis Arnulfi patris supradicte Lietgardis comitisse, Theo
2 CONC derici comitis…"[136].  The Iohannis de Thilrode Chronicon records the donation dated 962 by "Wicmannus comes…pro remedio anima coniugis mea Lietgardis…Arnulphi marchisi Flandrie patris" of "villam Thessela…Desselbergine" to "mona
2 CONC sterio Sancti Petri in Blandino"[137].  
2 CONT *The Annales Blandinienses record the deaths in 962 of "Baldwinus, filius Arnulfi marchisi, et soror eius Liutgardis"[138].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([after 10 Jul 953]) WICHMANN [V] Graaf van Hamaland, son of --- [Billung] & his wife Gerberga --- ([930]-after 27 Sep 979). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.   BAUDOUIN de Flandres ([935/40]-Abbey of St Bertin 1 Jan 962).  
2 CONT *His parentage is specified in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin[139].  "…Baldwini filii Arnulfi marchysi…" signed the charter dated 8 Jul 941 under which "Arnulfus…regis…marchysus" restored property to Saint-Pierre de Gand[140].  "A
2 CONC rnulfus Flandrie comes et marchisus" granted use of property "Snellenghem in pago Flandrensi" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for "uxore mea…Adala atque…filio meo Balduino et filia mea Lietgardis" and for deceased "Balduino genitore meo 
2 CONC et Elstrudis genetrice mea atque Heeberto filio meo", by charter dated 10 Jul 953[141].  
2 CONT *He ruled with his father from 958[142] as BAUDOUIN III Joint Count of Flanders and Artois, his father granting him the administration of the south of the county[143].  
2 CONT *A charter dated to 20 Jan [958/61] records the peace settlement agreed by "Baulduin…Marquis" between the abbey of Saint-Pierre de Gand and the avoués of Douchy, although this document is unlikely to be contemporary in the form sh
2 CONC own in the compilation as it is written in old French[144].  The Annales Blandinienses record the deaths in 962 of "Baldwinus, filius Arnulfi marchisi, et soror eius Liutgardis"[145].  The Annales Egmundani record the death in 962
2 CONC  of "Baldwinus filius Arnulfi marchisi Flandrensium"[146].  
2 CONT *m ([951/59]) as her first husband, MECHTILD of Saxony, daughter of HERMANN Billung Duke in Saxony & his [first/second] wife [Oda ---/Hildesuit ---] ([942]-Gent 25 May 1008, bur Gent St Peter).  "Mathilda Saxonici generic" is name
2 CONC d as wife of Count Baudouin in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin[147].  The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Bennonis ducis, qui et Bernhardus et Liudigeri comitis et Machtildis comitisse" as brothers and sister of "domna Suanehildis
2 CONC  [filia] Herimanni ducis de Liuniburh", recording the names of Mechtild's two husbands[148].  The Genealogica Arnulfi Comitis names "Mathildis, filiam principis Herimanni" as wife of "Balduinum [filius comitis Arnulfi]", specifyin
2 CONC g that it was hoped the couple would have many children[149].  This suggests that their marriage date may have been some years earlier than 961 considering that the Genealogia was supposedly compiled in [951/59], probably during t
2 CONC he earlier part of this date range considering which children of Louis IV King of the West Franks are named in the document[150].  Mechtild married secondly ([963]) Godefroi Comte de Verdun [Wigeriche] (-3/4 Sep after 995, bur Gen
2 CONC t St Peter).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Mathildis comitissa Saxonie" as wife of "Godefridi Ardennensis"[151].  The Annales Blandinienses record the death in 1008 of "Mathildis comitissa"[152].  The necrolo
2 CONC gy of Lüneburg records the death "25 May" of "Mattild com"[153].  
2 CONT *Baudouin III & his wife had one child.
2 CONT *Baudouin III had one possible illegitimate son by an unknown mistress.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. EGBERT de Flandre (-before 10 Jul 953).  
2 CONT *"Arnulfus Flandrie comes et marchisus" granted use of property "Snellenghem in pago Flandrensi" to Saint-Pierre de Gand, for "uxore mea…Adala atque…filio meo Balduino et filia mea Lietgardis" and for deceased "Balduino genitore m
2 CONC eo et Elstrudis genetrice mea atque Heeberto filio meo", by charter dated 10 Jul 953[157].  Egbert´s absence from the charter dated 8 Jul 941, under which "Arnulfus…regis…marchysus" restored property to Saint-Pierre de Gand, signe
2 CONC d by "…Baldwini filii Arnulfi marchysi…"[158], suggests that he must have been a younger son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  ELSTRUDE de Flandre (-966[159] or after).  
2 CONT *The Historia Comitum Ghisnensium names "comes Balduinus sororem…Elstrudem" as wife of "Sifridus"[160].  According to the Chronica Monasterii Sancti Bertini, the couple were never married[161].  
2 CONT *m ([960/65]) SIEGFRIED Comte de Guines, son of --- (-[965]). 
2 CONT
