2 CONT
2 CONT Bethóc ingen Maíl Coluim meic Cináeda was the eldest daughter of King Máel Coluim mac Cináeda, King of Scots, who had no known sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT The strongest hereditary claim of succession to the Scottish throne therefore passed through Bethóc. Approximately 1000, Princess Bethóc married Crínán, Abbot of Dunkeld. The first son of this marriage was Donnchad I, who ascended
2 CONC  to the throne of Scotland in 1034. Early writers have asserted that Máel Coluim also designated Donnchad as his successor under the rules of tanistry because there were other possible claimants to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her sister Olith was married to Jarl Sigurd the Stout of Orkney, and the other sister Donada to Findláech, the Mormaer of Moireabh.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is not to be confused with Bethóc ingen Domnaill Bain meic Donnchada.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Anderson, Marjorie Ogilvy. Kings and Kingship in Early Scotland, 1973 
2 CONT >>><nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT She gained the title of Heiress of Scone. As a result of her marriage, Bethoc of Scotland was styled as Lady of Atholl.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>><nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethoc (Beatrix) Princess of Scotland *-9942 [Parents] was born about 984 in of Atholl,Perthshire,Scotland. She married Crinan de Mormaer *-9941 about 1010 in of,Atholl,Perthshire,Scotland. The marriage ended in divorce.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT       		F 	i 	Daughter Mormaer Princess of Scotland +-9943 was born about 1011 in of Atholl,Perthshire,Scotland.
2 CONT       		M 	ii 	Duncan King of Scotland *-9932
2 CONT       		M 	iii 	Maldred Earl of Dunbar King of Cumbria *-9899
2 CONT
