2 CONT Bethóc was the wife of Crínán: CRINAN "the Thane", son of --- (-killed in battle 1045). Abthane of Dule. Lay abbot of Dunkeld. Steward of the Western Isles. Mormaer of Atholl. He was killed fighting King Macbeth. m ([1000]) BETHOC
2 CONC , daughter of MALCOLM II King of Scotland & his wife ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Genealogy of King William the Lyon" dated 1175 names
2 CONT
2 CONT "Betoch filii Malcolmi" as parent of "Malcolmi filii Dunecani"[131].
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of the Scots and Picts dated 1177 names
2 CONT
2 CONT "Cran Abbatis de Dunkelden et Bethok filia Malcolm mac Kynnet" as parents of King Duncan[132].
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of John of Fordun records that King Malcolm II had
2 CONT
2 CONT "an only daughter…Beatrice who married Crynyne Abthane of Dul and Steward of the Isles…in some annals, by a blunder of the writer…abbot of Dul"[133].
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady of Atholl. (Cawley's Medlands)
2 CONT
2 CONT Crinan & Bethoc had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i) DUNCAN ([1001]-killed in battle either Bothganowan/Pitgaveny, near Elgin, or Burghead 14 Aug 1040, bur Isle of Iona). His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Ulster which record the death of "Donnchad son of Crínán, king of
2 CONC  Scotland" in 1040[209]. The Chronicle of John of Fordun names "Duncan" as son of "Crynyne Abthane of Dul and Steward of the Isles" and his wife[210]. He succeeded in 1018 as King of Strathclyde. He succeeded his maternal grandfat
2 CONC her in 1034 as DUNCAN I King of Scotland. (Cawley’s Medlands)
2 CONT
2 CONT ii) MALDRED (-killed in battle [1045]). His parentage is confirmed by Simeon of Durham who records the marriage of "Maldred the son of Crinan"[211]. Lord of Allerdale. Regent of Strathclyde 1034/35. (Cawley’s Medlands)
2 CONT
