2 CONT
2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: Young; Kraentzler 1406, 1409; AF;  A. Roots 239; History of Morgan Family.
2 CONT    Roots: Angharat of Tegaingl, daughter of Owain ap Edwin.
2 CONT    Young: Angharad II of Tegaingl.
2 CONT    K: Anghared verch Owain (the Golden Hair).
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT   1.  Lloyd, John E., _The History of Wales, Vol. II:
2 CONT P. 464: "By his wife Angharad, the flaxen-haired daughter of Owain ab Edwin, whom he married about 1095, he had three sons, Cadwallon, Owain, and Cadwaladr, and five daughters...." Footnote 7, same page, names the daughters as Gwe
2 CONC nllian (wife of Gruffydd ap Rhys), Marared, Rannillt (named for her paternal grandmother), Susanna (who married Madog ap Maredudd), and Annest.
2 CONT P. 488: Owain Gwynedd fell into a deep melancholy when his mother died in 1162.
2 CONT
2 CONT   2.  Family Group Record.
