2 CONT
2 CONT Leofwine (c. 950 – 1028), was an ealdorman in Mercia. He is mentioned as Wicciarum Prouinciarum dux[1] (Ealdorman of Hwicce) in 997.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leofwine may have been related by marriage to the family of Ælfgifu of Northampton.[2] The chronicles mention four children of Leofwine, their order of birth is unknown:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Northman, killed in 1017.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Edwin, killed in battle in 1039.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Godwin, died some time before 1056.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Leofric, Earl of Mercia.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Notes
2 CONT
