2 CONT I found this information online at the Wikipedia site.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lived in Northumberland, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Leofwine (c. 950 – 1028) was an ealdorman of the Hwicce in Mercia. He is mentioned as Wicciarum Prouinciarum dux[1] Ealdorman of Hwicce in 997.
2 CONT
2 CONT The chronicles mention four children of Leofwine, their order of birth is unknown:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Northman, killed in 1017.[2]
2 CONT     Eadwine, killed in battle in 1039.[2]
2 CONT     Godwine, died some time before 1056.[3]
2 CONT     Leofric, Earl of Mercia.
2 CONT
2 CONT I found this information online at the Wikipedia site.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Leofwine de Ardenne, Earl of Mercia
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Leofwine (died in or after 1023) was appointed Ealdorman of the Hwicce by King Æthelred II of England in 994. The territory of the Hwicce was a kingdom in the western midlands in the early Anglo-Saxon period, which soon became a s
2 CONC ubdivision of Mercia. Leofwine was the son of Ælfwine, who is otherwise unknown, but the family appears to come from the east midlands. Leofwine and his sons were remembered by the Worcester church as spoliators who seized church 
2 CONC land, but as benefactors by east midlands religious establishments.
2 CONT
2 CONT Under Æthelred, Leofwine's sphere of office was in the Hwicce areas of Worcestershire and Gloucestershire, but these counties were given to Danes by King Cnut soon after he gained the throne in 1016. However, Leofwine kept his ran
2 CONC k and may have been appointed Ealdorman of Mercia in 1017 in succession to Eadric Streona, but Leofwine's eldest son Northman was murdered on Cnut's orders in the same year. Leofwine is last recorded as a charter witness in 1023 a
2 CONC nd probably died soon afterwards. His son Leofric was Earl of Mercia by 1032. Leofwine had two others sons, Edwine, who died at the Battle of Rhyd-y-groes in 1039, and Godwine.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Northman Leofricsson de Ardenne, Dux de Wicciarum
