2 CONT Cerdic was a Saxon earldorman who founded a settlement on the coast ofHampshire, England, in 495, assumed the title of King of the West Saxonsin 519, and became the ancestor of the English royal line.
1 NOTE He is a shadowy figure in early Wessex history, mentioned only in the regnal list in the preface of the Anglo-Saxon chronicle. There he is stated to have been the son of Cerdic and father to Cynric.
