2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ælfthryth (?) (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #102422, b. circa 945, d. circa 17 November 1002
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=4 Dec 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT      Ælfthryth (?) was born circa 945 at Lydford Castle, Devon, England. (2) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Ordgar, Ealdorman of Devon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Æthelwold, Ealdorman of East Anglia, son of Æthelstan, Ealdorman, between 962 and 963. (3)
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Eadgar 'the Peaceful', King of England, son of Eadmund I, King of England and Ælfgifu (?), between 964 and 965. (2) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa 17 November 1002 at Wherwell Abbey, Hampshire, England. (3)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Ælfthryth (?) was also known as Alstrita (?). (2) She was also known as Elstrudis (?). (3) From 11 May 973, her married name became Queen Elfrida of England. (3) She was a nun circa 986 at Wherwell Abbey, Hampshire, England. 
2 CONC (3)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ælfthryth (?) and Æthelwold, Ealdorman of East Anglia
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Edgar (?) b. bt 962 - 9643
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Ethelfleda (?) b. c 963, d. c 10163
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ælfthryth (?) and Eadgar 'the Peaceful', King of England
2 CONT
