2 CONT Ælfthryth was born circa 945 in Lydford Castle, Devon, England.2 She was the daughter of Ordgar, Ealdorman of Devon. She married, firstly, Æthelwold, Ealdorman of East Anglia, son of Æthelstan, Ealdorman, between 962 and 963.3 She
2 CONC  married, secondly, Eadgar 'the Peaceful', King of England, son of Eadmund I, King of England and Ælfgifu, between 964 and 965.2 She died circa 17 November 1002 in Wherwell Abbey, Hampshire, England.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Ælfthryth was also known as Alstrita.2 She was also known as Elstrudis.3 From 11 May 973, her married name became Queen Elfrida of England.3 She was a nun circa 986 Wherwell Abbey, Hampshire.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 Æthelwold, Ealdorman of East Anglia d. 963 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Edgar b. bt 962 - 9643 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethelfleda b. c 963, d. c 10163 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 Eadgar 'the Peaceful', King of England b. between 942 and 944, d. 8 July 975 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Edmund Atheling b. c 965, d. bt 970 - 9724 
2 CONT
2 CONT Æthelred II 'the Unready', King of England+ b. bt 966 - 969, d. 23 Apr 10164 
