2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first marriage was to Ethelwald, Ealdorman of East Anglia around 962-963. She is said to have had an affair with King Edgar while married to Ethelwald.  Some sources assert that Ethelwald was murdered on Edgar's orders.  She w
2 CONC as crowned with Edgar on 5/11/973 at Bath Abbey.  This was the first instance of the coronation of a Queen in England.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She became a nun circa 986 at Wherwell Abbey in Hampshire where she died possibly on 11/17/1002 (she was alive in 999 but had died before the end of 1002).
2 CONT
2 CONT It is probable that her husband's successor, Edward (his son by his first wife, Ethelfleda the Fair) was murdered on her orders at Corfe Castle, Dorset, thus enabling her son, Ethelred, to assume the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT 973-75 Joint Ruler Queen Ælfthryth of England
2 CONT
2 CONT 978-84 Regent Dowager Queen
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources indicated that after her consecration she was considered to been sharing the royal lordship with her husband, King Edgar, who was first succeeded by his son of the first marriage, Edward, then by a brother, and finally by 
2 CONC his son by Ælfthryth, Edmund II Ironside (968-78-1016), and was in charge of the government during his minority, and continued to be a dominant force after he came of age [http://www.guide2womenleaders.com/womeninpower/Womeninpowe
2 CONC -chronological1.htm].
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86lfthryth,_Queen_of_England
2 CONT
2 CONT Ælfthryth (c.945 to c.1000, also Alfrida, Elfrida or Elfthryth) was the second or third wife of King Edgar of England. Ælfthryth was the first king's wife known to have been crowned and anointed as Queen of the Kingdom of England.
2 CONC  Mother of King Æthelred the Unready, she was a powerful political figure. She was linked to the murder of her stepson King Edward the Martyr and appeared as a stereotypical bad queen and evil stepmother in many medieval histories
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ælfthryth,_wife_of_Edgar
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ælfthryth (c. 945-1000, also Alfrida, Elfrida or Elfthryth) was the second or third wife of King Edgar of England. Ælfthryth was the first king's wife known to have been crowned and anointed as Queen of the Kingdom of England. Mot
2 CONC her of King Ethelred the Unready, she was a powerful political figure. She was linked to the murder of her stepson King Edward the Martyr and appeared as a stereotypical bad Queen and evil stepmother in many medieval histories.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ælfthryth of Devon
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Æthelwold (no children)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Edgar "the Peaceable" King of England (his second wife), two sons: Edmund and Æthelred
