2 CONT === Spouses ===
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Gilbert, Duke of Lorraine.
2 CONT Children: Alberade of Lorraine b. about 929. Married Renaud (originally as Ragenold), a Viking chieftain who became the Count of Roucy [1] Henri, Duke of Lorraine b. about 932 Gerberge of Lorraine b. about 935. Married Adalbert I 
2 CONC of Vermandois. Wiltrude, b. about 937.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Louis IV of France in 939. Children: Lothair of France (941-986) Mathilde b. about 943; married Conrad of Burgundy Hildegarde b. about 944 Carloman b. about 945 Louis b. about 948 Charles, Duke of Lower Lorraine (953-993) Alber
2 CONC ade b. before 953 Henri b. about 953
2 CONT
2 CONT GERBERGA (Nordhausen [913/14] -Reims 5 May 984, bur Abbaye de Reims). Liutprand states that the wife of "Gislebertum Lotharingorum ducem" was "regis sororem" [164]. Flodoard names her "Gerbergam" when recording her second marriage
2 CONC  [165]. Her first husband had been a rival of King Heinrich I and maybe planned to establish himself as independent ruler in Lotharingia in 920 [166]. As the marriage coincided with Giselbert being created dux, it was presumably a
2 CONC rranged to confirm Giselbert's submission to King Heinrich. King Louis married Gerberga without the permission of her brother Otto I King of Germany, probably to increase his hold on Lotharingia (ruled by her first husband). Gerbe
2 CONC rga was active in the defense of Laon in 941 and of Reims in 946,accompanied her husband on expeditions to Aquitaine in 944 and Burgundy in 949, and was active during his period of imprisonment in 945/46 [167]. An educated person,
2 CONC  she commissioned from Adso of Moutier-en-Der the De ortu et tempore antichristi [168]. Her second husband gave her the abbey of Notre-Dame de Laon in 951, taken from his mother on her second marriage. Abbess of Notre Dame de Sois
2 CONC sons in 959 [169].
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([928/29]) GISELBERT Graf [von Maasgau], son of REGINAR [I] "Langhals" Graaf [van Maasgau] Comte de Hainaut & his wife Alberada --- (-drowned in the River Rhine Oct 929) . He was created dux in 928 by Heinrich I King of 
2 CONC Germany, which effectively created him GISELBERT Duke of Lotharingia.
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (end 939) LOUIS IV "d'Outremer" King of the West Franks, son of CHARLES III "le Simple" King of the West Franks & his second wife Eadgifu [Ogive] of England ([10 Sep 920/10 Sep 921] -Reims Oct 954, bur Reims St Remy).
2 CONT
