1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gunnar von Arnold notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sohn des Burggrafen Babo I. von Regensburg aus seiner 3. Ehe mit der Mathilde (Prinz Isenburg)  ''(Son of Babo and Mathilde in his third marriage)''  [http://www.genealogie-mittelalter.de/babonen_burggrafen_von_regensburg/liudolf_
2 CONC moench.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Liudolf 
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT F. und einmaliges Vorkommen (996): Liutolf Sohn Babos, tritt als Mönch in St. Emmeram ein nQ 8, 214 n 256. 
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT Liudolf trat um 996 ins Kloster St. Emmeran in Regensburg ein. Er fungierte 972/76 zusammen mit seinem Vater Babo als Vogt für einen Priester Ellinpreht, welcher Besitz im Raume Erding, Vilsbiburg, Ebersberg vertauschte. 977/94 be
2 CONC gegnete Liudolf allein als Vogt für einen Kleriker Reginfrid im gleichen geographischen Raum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT GvA: This, however, does not explain the years written above "He worked , with his father; as ... In antoher source Liudolf was born 996, five years after Babo and Mathildes marriage. Tricky...working on it. But I moved Liudolf to
2 CONC  Mathildes branch as a starter /Gunnar
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT I don't think any of this "ancestors" children have a source about being fathered by Liudolf (they aren't in the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy passage about Liudolf). So I have to presume that the mother is a GEDCOM file. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Looking forward to reviewing documentation on the children, meanwhile.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Liudolf, Duke of Swabia
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Liudolf married Ida, daughter of Duke Herman I.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son by Ida, Otto, was later duke of Bavaria and Swabia, his daughter Mathilde abess of a canoness monastery in Essen.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT See text on Babo von Babenberg (Burggrafen von regensburg)
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage of Babo and Ita is a theory, better described in the profile of Babo
