2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Medlands page on Carinthia (focusing on the succession in Carinthia):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CARINTHIA.htm#OttoWormsDukeCarinthiadied1004
2 CONT
2 CONT DUKES of CARINTHIA (DUKES of FRANCONIA)
2 CONT
2 CONT OTTO I 978-985, 995-1002, KONRAD I 1004-1011, KONRAD II 1036-1039
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. OTTO von Franken, son of KONRAD "der Rote" Duke of Lotharingia, Graf in Franconia & his wife Liutgard of Germany (-4 Nov 1004, bur [Bruchsal]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Ottonem" as son of "duci Wormatie Conrado", specifying that he was father of "Cono dux et Henricus pater imperatoris Conradi"[7].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf im Nahegau 956.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf im Speier-, Worms-, Elsenz-, Kraich-, Engpfinz- und Ufgau.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was installed as OTTO Duke of Carinthia by Otto II King of Germany in 978 after the trial of Heinrich Duke of Carinthia who had been implicated in the rebellion of Heinrich II "der Zänker" Duke of Bavaria against the king[8].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Otto was deprived of Carinthia in 985 when it was returned to Duke Heinrich I [Liutpoldinger], but allowed to retain the ducal title and granted lands around Worms and Frankfurt[9].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Restored from 995 to 1002. 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)   Other children: see FRANCONIA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)   KONRAD (-12 or 15 Dec 1011, bur Worms cathedral).  
2 CONT *Herimannus names "Counradus dux Carentani, filius Ottonis ducis fraterque Brunonis dudum papæ" when recording his death in 1012[10].  
2 CONT *He was candidate for the imperial throne in 1002.  
2 CONT *He was installed as KONRAD I Duke of Carinthia in 1004. 
2 CONT *He had one son, Konrad II "der Jungere", Duke of Carinthia (b. c1003, d. 20 July 1039, b. Worms Cathedral
2 CONT
