1 NOTE Acceded 975-979.
1 NOTE He succeeded his Father in 975 and died unmarried and without issue. He was murdered by his stepmother, Elfrida at Corfe Castle and was interred at Shaftesbury Castle. An archaeological dig in 1931 at Shaftsbury Abbey unearthed bo
2 CONC nes believed to be those of Edward. A dispute over possession and re-burial led to the remains being deposited in a branch of the Midland Bank in Croydon, Surrey where they remained until recently; reburial may have been achieved.
2 CONC  Succeeded by his half-brother. {Burke�s Peerage and other sources} [GADD.GED]
