2 CONC  leadership of the England was divided, some supporting Edward's claim to be king and other supporting his much younger half-brother Æthelred. Edward was chosen as king and was crowned by his main clerical supporters, Archbishops 
2 CONC Dunstan and Oswald of Worcester.
