1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HOLLAND.htm#DirkIA :
2 CONT
2 CONT HERLINDE .  The Chronologia Johannes de Beke names (in order) "Arnulfum comitem, Egbertum Treverensem archiepiscopum ac Arlindam puellam" as the children of Count Dirk II & his wife[281].  The Annales Egmundani name "Erlinda soror
2 CONC  eius [=Ekbertus filius Theoderici II comitis] monocula"[282].  The Vita Sancti Adalberti Egmondani names "eidem comiti [=Theoderici iunioris] filia Erlinda"[283].  Abbess of Egmont, later of Bennsbrock.  The reference in the Anna
2 CONC les Egmundani to her being one-eyed provides an interesting corroboration for the theory that children with disabilities were assigned to careers in the church. 
