3 CONT
3 CONT Gruffydd ap Cynan was born in Ireland of the royal line of Gwynedd and made several attempts to regain Gwynedd before finally succeeding.
3 CONT
3 CONT Much of his kingdom was overrun by Normans, who imprisoned him but he escaped to join the anti-Norman rebellion of 1094.
3 CONT
3 CONT Driven out again in 1098, he retired to Ireland, but returned as a ruler of Anglesey.
