2 CONC 0 of “Gormlaith, daughter of Murchad son of Fland” mother of “Sitric son of Olaf king of the Foreigners and of Donnchad son of Brian king of Munster”[850].  Brian must have separated from his wife Gormlaith if the reference to his
2 CONC  wife Dub is correct, unless the marriages were polygamous.  She married thirdly, as his [third] wife, Maelsechnaill King of Ireland.  The Annals of the Four Masters record the death in 1030 of “Gormlaith daughter of Murchadh son 
2 CONC of Finn, mother of the king of the foreigners Sitric, Donnchadh son of Brian king of Munster, and Conchobhar son of Maeleachlainn king of Teamhair”[851]. 
