2 CONT >Devout" Fitzharding (abt 1095-1170) (who is also listed as the son of 
2 CONT >Prince Harding of Denmark, m. to Livida) (Gloucestershire, Eng) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT You can break the genealogy at the above generation. According to the 
2 CONT 'Complete Peerage' vol II pp 124-129, which is pretty reliable, 
2 CONT Maurice de Berkeley's parents were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert fitz Harding, lord of Berkeley (c1095-5 Feb 1170/71), who was 
2 CONT possibly a merchant of Bristol, and Eve, Prioress of St Michael's 
2 CONT Hill, Bristol (?-12 Mar 1170). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT CP gives no parentage for Eve (and the one above looks incredibly 
2 CONT dodgy) and says Robert was the son of Harding (as the name suggests), 
2 CONT but nowhere mentions that he was a prince (also unlikely). CP does say 
2 CONT that Harding might have been son of Eadnoth the Staller, who was 
2 CONT killed in 1068. 
2 CONT (Chris Phillips's message elsewhere in the thread refers to more 
2 CONT recent research on Robert). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >son Maurice "The Make Peace" Fitzrobert Fitzharding, (abt 1120-1190), m. 
2 CONT >Alice de Berkeley, (abt 1135-1190) (Bristol, Gloucestershire; Berkeley, 
2 CONT >Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Am having trouble authenticating the link to William from a true source. Here the dates don't add up. So while everything else prior to this link is true the link itself may not be,
