2 CONT >>a)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Erling-of-Orkneys/6000000003820968908 ERLING] (-[Ulster [May] 1103]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Erling and Magnus” as the two sons of “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” and his wife “Thora, the daught
2 CONC er of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”[908].  Jarl of Orkney.  Orkneyinga Saga states that “according to some people, Erling, the son of Earl Erlend, was killed in the battle of the Menai Straits, but Snorri Sturluson says that he met his dea
2 CONC th with King Magnus in Ulster”[909].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>b)         [http://www.geni.com/people/St-Magnus-Erlendsson/6000000008248157090 St MAGNUS] Erlendsson (-murdered Egilsay 16 Apr [1117], bur Christchurch at Birsay, transferred to Kirkwall Cathedral).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>c)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Erlendottir/6000000001169154976 GUNHILD].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m (Spring 1099) [http://www.geni.com/people/Kol-Kali-Lalisson/6000000001169130795?through=6000000001169154976  KOL] Kalisson, son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-S%C3%A6bj%C3%B8rnson/6000000003820968938?through=6000000001169
2 CONC 130795  KALI] of Agdir in Norway & his wife ---.  Lenderman in Agder.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>d)         [http://www.geni.com/people/Cecilia-Erlendsdatter/6000000008177258360  CECILIA].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m [http://www.geni.com/people/Isaac-of-Orkneys/6000000008177322586?through=6000000008177258360 ISAAC]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Erlend had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:    
2 CONT
