2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cr%C3%ADn%C3%A1n_of_Dunkeld
2 CONT
2 CONT Crinán's second son, Maldred of Allerdale, held the title of Lord of Cumbria. It is said that from him, the Earls of Dunbar, for example Patrick Dunbar, 9th Earl of Dunbar, descend in unbroken male line.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT MALDRED, son of CRINAN "the Thane" Mormaer of Atholl [Scotland] & his wife Bethoc of Scotland Lady of Atholl (-killed in battle [1045]).  He is named son of Crinan by Roger of Hoveden[379].  Lord of Allerdale.  Regent of Strathcly
2 CONC de 1034/35. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([before 1040]) EALDGYTH [Ælfgifu], daughter and heiress of UHTRED Earl of Northumbria & his third wife Ælfgifu of England (1016 or before-).  Simeon of Durham names "Algiva daughter of earl Uchtred [and] of Algiva daughter of k
2 CONC ing Agelred" when recording that her father arranged her marriage to "Maldred the son of Crinan"[380], although her father was long since dead when she married.  Named daughter of Uhtred and Elgiva by Roger of Hoveden, who also na
2 CONC mes her husband and his father[381]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Maldred & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GOSPATRICK ([1040/48]-[1075]).  Simeon of Durham names "Cospatric son of Maldred son of Crinan" when recording that he was appointed Earl of Northumberland[382].  Earl of Northumberland from Dec 1067. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         MALDRED .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   m ---.  The name of Maldred´s wife is not known.  Maldred & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         UHTRED .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   m ---.  The name of Uhtred´s wife is not known.  Uhtred & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          [383]DOLFIN .  The Prior of Durham granted him Staindrop (in which Raby is a township) in 1131[384].  m ---.  The name of Dolfin´s wife is not known.  Dolfin & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       [385]MALDRED .  m ---.  The name of Maldred´s wife is not known.  Maldred & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       [386]ROBERT FitzMaldred (-[25 Jun 1242/26 May 1248]).  Lord of Raby and Brancepeth, co. Durham.  m as her first husband, ISABEL de Neville, daughter of GEOFFREY de Neville & his wife Emma de Bulmer (-before May 1254).  S
2 CONC he was heiress of her brother Henry de Neville.  She married secondly Gilbert de Brakenberg.  Robert & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a.         GEOFFREY FitzRobert (-1242).  He assumed the name Neville after his mother's family.   
2 CONT
2 CONT -         see ENGLISH NOBILITY. EARLS of WESTMORELAND (NEVILLE). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         [GOSPATRICK .  "…Cospatric filius Uctred…" witnessed inquisitions by "David…Cumbrensis regionis princeps", dated 1124, concerning land owned by the church of Glasgow[387].]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Maldred, Lord of Allerdale was born circa 1015 at Dunbar, Scotland.3 He was the son of Crinan, Mormaer of Atholl and Bethoc of Scotland.2 He married Ealdgyth (?), daughter of Uhtred, Earl of Northumberland and Ælfgifu (?), circa 1
2 CONC 036.3 He died in 1045, killed in action, while attempting to avenge the murder of his brother by Macbeth.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      Maldred, Lord of Allerdale gained the title of Lord of Allerdale [Feudal].4 He held the office of Regent of the Kingdom of Strathclyde between 1034 and 1045.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maldred, Lord of Allerdale and Ealdgyth (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Maldred (?)+ 5
2 CONT
2 CONT     * unknown of Scotland+ 5
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Gospatric, Earl of Northumberland+ b. c 1040, d. c 10752
