2 CONT 6.    OWAIN I GWYNEDD, b. ca. 1100, d. 1170, Prince of North Wales; m. (1) GLADYS (176-5); m. (2) Christina (his cousin), dau. Bronw ap Owen ap Edwin.  (Arthur Jones: History of Gruffydd ap Cynan, Manchester, 1910, a translation a
2 CONC nd analysis of a twelfth century biography of Griffith, is the source for this
2 CONT pedigree, with details verified and amplified from the Irish Annals, especially the Annals of Innisfallen, of Ulster, and of the Four Masters).
