0 @N6000000003949663823@ NOTE He is the eponymous founder of Ceredigion.  His existence is subject to doubt.  He must have been a younger son of Cunedda as Einion inherited the heartland of Venedotia.  He probably ruled it as a sub kingdom of Gwynedd.
1 CONT Ceredig was born in his father Cunedda Wledig’s original homeland of Manau Gododdin around the Upper Firth of Forth. When called upon to expel Irish invaders from North Wales in the early 5th century, he travelled south, with the 
1 CONC rest of his family. He fought bravely against the advancing Gaels and his father rewarded him with the most southern area of his new kingdom, bordering on Dyfed, possibly including part of the Cantref Gwaelod. The region became so
1 CONC  associated with Ceredig that the people named it Ceredigion after him.   (per EBK Bios)
