1 CONT
1 CONT It is assumed that Cynfarch ruled in Rheged before Urien. Accepting H.M. Chadwick's suggestion that Senyllt ap Dingad was a king of Galloway, expelled to the Isle of Man around 550, David Nash Ford suggests that Cynfarch was his o
1 CONC ppressor. Hence the apparent 'Rheged' placename at Dunragit near Stranraer and tales of Mark ap Meirchion (or Cun-mark ap Meirchion) in the same area. He may also have been a participant in the Battle of Arfderydd in 573. Galloway
1 CONC  (Scottish Gaelic, Gall-ghaidhealaibh or Gallobha, Lowland Scots Gallowa) today refers to the former counties of Wigtownshire and the Stewartry of Kirkcudbright in southwest Scotland, but has fluctuated greatly in size over histor
1 CONC y. ... Events By Place Byzantine Empire Silk reaches Constantinople (approximate date). ... Dunragit is a village on the A75, between Stranraer and Glenluce in Dumfries and Galloway (previously Wigtownshire) in south-west Scotland
