0 @N6000000003658772375@ NOTE CUNEDDA, called Gwledig, or Over-King, the perpetuator of the command and authority of the Dux Britanniarum. He was the first native ruler of the Cymry after the retirement of the Romans in 410. His power extended from Carlisle to
1 CONC  Wearmouth, his court being held at the former place. His retinue consisted of 900 horse, and he wore the golden belt and other insignia of the office of Over-King. He was a fervent Catholic, and converted his subjects to Christia
1 CONC nity; his descendants were, many of them, ecclesiastics, who organised the Church in his Kingdom. Cunedda left issue eight sons
1 CONT
1 CONT WIKIPEDIA:
