0 @N6000000002187905632@ NOTE Einion Yrth ap Cunedda
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Einion ap Cunedda (c.420 - 500; reigned from the 470s) (Latin: Engenius; English: Enoch), also known as Einion Yrth ('the Impetuous') was a king of Gwynedd. One of the sons of Cunedda, it is believed he traveled with his father to
1 CONC  North Wales in the early 450s to expel Irish raiders from the region. After his father's death, Einion inherited control over the newly founded kingdom of Gwynedd. Aided by his brother Ceredig, ruler of Ceredigion, and his nephew
1 CONC  Meirion, ruler of Meirionnydd, Einion built upon his father's successes and further established his family's rule in the region. He was succeeded by two sons; Cadwallon Lawhir and Owain Ddantgwyn.
1 CONT
1 CONT In a theory by David Sims and Mick Baker Einion Yrth is none other than Uther Pendragon or rather Yrthr Pen Draig.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Cunedda Wledig Kings of Gwynedd Followed by:
1 CONT Cadwallon Lawhir
0 @N6000000001745124928@ NOTE EINION YRTH (son of No. 1). The appellation "Yrth" is believed to indicate that he was of a
1 CONT           hasty and impetuous temperament. In the division of the kingdom the portion of Einion was in
1 CONT           Gwynedd. No record of his deeds or misdeeds has been preserved.
1 CONT
1 CONT (Lucius Weaver, The Weaver Genealogy, 1928)
0 @N6000000002188329867@ NOTE Einion Yrth, King of Gwynedd
1 CONT (Born c.AD 419)
1 CONT (Latin: Engenius; English: Enoch)
1 CONT
1 CONT Einion Yrth (the Impetuous) originated in Manau Gododdin on the Firth of Forth. He travelled to North Wales with his father, Cunedda Wledig, in the early 5th century to expel the invading Irish. Despite, apparently, being the seve
1 CONC nth son, he must have been of strong character for he became heir to his father's central power-base of Gwynedd. The kingdom was named after the Irish people known, in Latin, as the Venodotæ. From here, Einion was eventually able 
1 CONC to impose himself as over-king to most of his brothers.
1 CONT
1 CONT
