0 @N6000000002188039146@ NOTE Dumnagual I of Alt Clut
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Dumnagual I of Alt Clut or simply Dumnagual Hen ("the Old") was the ruler of Alt Clut (modern Dumbarton Rock), probably sometime in the early sixth century. According to the Harleian genealogies, he was the son of a Cinuit, the so
1 CONC n of King Ceretic of Alt Clut. He is known to have fathered several sons, including the future King Clinoch and Guipno, the father of the future king Neithon of Alt Clut.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT References
1 CONT MacQuarrie, Alan, "The Kings of Strathclyde", in A. Grant & K.Stringer (eds.) Medieval Scotland: Crown, Lordship and Community, Essays Presented to G.W.S. Barrow, (Edinburgh, 1993), pp. 1-19. 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT External links
1 CONT Harleian genealogy 5 
1 CONT David Nash Ford's "Early British Kingdoms" 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
