0 @N6000000002187592040@ NOTE Gabhran of Dalriada
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Gabhran (Scottish Gaelic: Gabhran mac Domangart) was king of Dál Riada from about 538 until 558.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gabhran was a wise and excellent Prince. He first instituted the office of the King's Advocate. He persuaded Loth, a Pictish King, to league with Uther Pendragon, King of the Britons against the Anglo-Saxons in 502. Loth was also 
1 CONC persuaded to marry Ann-Morgause, daughter to Gorlois and Igraine, step-daughter to the Pendragon and elder half-sister to King Arthur of the Round Table. When the famous King Arthur mounted the British throne, Gabhran aided him ag
1 CONC ainst the Saxons.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gabhran was at last cut off, for one Toncetus, the Supreme Judge of Capital Crimes, a cruel and covetous man, expecting easy pardon of the King; the enraged people therefore cut him off. But finding they could not obtain the King'
1 CONC s mercy, they next slew the King himself in 535 at the instigation of one Donald of Athol after a reign of thirty-four years.
1 CONT
1 CONT His Queen and children fled to Ireland. Others say that he died after a tedious sickness and was buried at Icolmkill, the royal burying place.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was succeeded by his nephew, Eugenius III, who instead of revenging his uncle's death, received Donald into favor, which made him suspected of having a hand in the conspiracy; and he was succeeded in 558 by his brother Conall, 
1 CONC who introduced heraldry.
1 CONT
1 CONT Conall recalled the children of Gabhran but died before their return in 568 after a reign of ten years. Conall was succeeded by his younger brother Kintellus, who courteously entertained Aedan of Dalriada, son of Gabhran and on hi
1 CONC s deathbed resigned to him.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Comgall King of Dál Riada
1 CONT 538-558 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Conall I 
