0 @N6000000002187592051@ NOTE Domangart I of Dalriada
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Domangart I (Scottish Gaelic: Domangart mac Fergus) was king of Dál Riada from about 501 until 507, following the death of his father, Fergus Mor. He may have joint ruled with his uncle, Aeneas.
1 CONT
1 CONT Domangart married Feldelm Foltchain, daughter of Brion son of Eochaid Mugmedon, a half-brother to the High King of Ireland Niall of the Nine Hostages. He has at least two sons: Comgall and Gabhran, both of whom became kings in suc
1 CONC cession. The Tripartite Life of St. Patrick states that he was present at the death of the saint, circa 493. Domangart died around 507 and was succeeded by Comgall.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Fergus I King of Dál Riada
1 CONT 501-507 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Comgall 
