1 CONT It is similarly recorded in the pedigree of the Kings of South Rheged in the Achau Brenhinoedd a Thywysogion Cymru as:
1 CONT
1 CONT Beli Mawr Beli Mawr (the Great) 
1 CONT Aflech Afallach, duplicate generations 
1 CONT Avallach 
1 CONT Enddolev Euddolen/Eudos/Eifudd, possible duplicate generations 
1 CONT Endos 
1 CONT Eneid 
1 CONT Endeyrn Eudeyrn/Euddigan, duplicate generations 
1 CONT Endigant 
1 CONT Rydeyrn Rhydeyrn 
1 CONT Rriuedel Rhifedel 
1 CONT Gradd Gratian 
1 CONT Vrban Urban 
1 CONT Tyddbwyll Telpwyll 
1 CONT Deheuwaint Deheuwaint/Tegfan or Tasciovanus, duplicate generations 
1 CONT Tegvan 
1 CONT Koel Godebawg Coel Hen (the Old) 
1 CONT
1 CONT Coel's father is thus shown to have born the native Celtic name of Tegfan. In Latin, this becomes Tasciovanus, a name known to have been in use in Britain during pre-Roman times, at least amongst the Catuvellauni tribe. Telpwyll i
1 CONC s an otherwise unknown name, probably Celtic, but the extended ancestry have distinctly Roman names (Urban and Gratian), before descending into corrupt mythology. Coel Hen evidently had a mixed racial background. He spawned a wide
1 CONC spread Northern dynasty.
