0 @N6000000002240813667@ NOTE Cenwalh married, then divorced the sister of Penda, the King of Mercia. Penda
1 CONT expelled Cenwalh because of the divorce to his sister, but after returning
1 CONT from Mercia, Cenwalh gained a victory over the Welsh near Pen-Selwood by
1 CONT which a large portion of Somerset came into his hands. In 661, he was again
1 CONT attacked by the Mercians, then under King Wulfhere. Cenwalh was in exile from
1 CONT 645-648, driven there by Penda for divorcing his sister.
