1 CONT    4. D. P. Kirby, The Earliest English Kings (1991), second edition (2000), Routledge, paperback, ISBN 0-415-24211-8.
1 CONT    5. Henry of Huntingdon, Historia Anglorum, translated by D. Greenway (1997), Oxford University Press.
1 CONT    6. M. Ziegler, "The Politics of Exile in Early Northumbria", The Heroic Age, Issue 2, Autumn/Winter 1999.
1 CONT    7. S. Bassett (ed.), The Origins of Anglo-Saxon Kingdoms (1989).
1 CONT    8. Bede, Ecclesiastical History of the English People (731), Book II and Book III.
1 CONT    9. N. J. Higham, The Convert Kings: Power and Religious Affiliation in Early Anglo-Saxon England (1997), pages 219, 240 and 241.
1 CONT   10. C. Stancliffe and E. Cambridge (ed.), Oswald: Northumbrian King to European Saint (1995, reprinted 1996), Paul Watkins, paperback.
1 CONT   11. D. J. V. Fisher, The Anglo-Saxon Age (1973), Longman, hardback, ISBN 0-582-48277-1, pages 66 and 117–118.
1 CONT   12. J. O. Prestwich, "King Æthelhere and the battle of the Winwaed," The English Historical Review, Vol. 83, No. 326 (January 1968), pages 89–95.
1 CONT   13. A. Breeze, "The Battle of the Uinued and the River Went, Yorkshire", Northern History, Vol. 41, Issue 2 (September 2004), pages 377–83.
