0 @N6000000002188314177@ NOTE Eoppa of Bernicia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Eoppa (died c. 547) was the father of Ida, who was the first king of Bernicia. The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle records him as the son of Esa and grandson of Ingwy.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Directory of Royal Genealogical Data, Brian C Tompsett; [1]
0 @N6000000002188314110@ NOTE Glappa of Bernicia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Glappa of Bernicia ruled from 559 to 560. He was the second known king of Bernicia.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was one of between 8 to 12 sons born to Ida of Bernicia, founder of the Anglo-Saxon kingdom of Bernicia. Nothing is known of his life and reign. The earliest authorities differ widely on the order and the regnal years of the ki
1 CONC ngs between the death of Ida and the beginning of Æthelfrith's rule (592/593).
