1 CONT ? Woolf, "Ungus". 
1 CONT ? Woolf, "Ungus". 
1 CONT ? AU s.a. 747; Forsyth, op. cit., pp. 21-22; Woolf, ibid.; Foster, "Discovery", pp. 42–43. 
1 CONT ? Henderson, ibid.; MacLean, "The Northumbrian Perspective", pp. 200-201; Woolf, op. cit. It is less certain whose remains the sarcophagus contained. Woolf and MacLean argue for Óengus while Henderson favours Nechtan mac Der Ilei.
1 CONC  See also Clancy, "Caustantín", favouring a 9th century dat
1 CONT ? Foster, ibid.; Broun, ibid. 
