1 CONC stantín son of Fergus (Uurgust)". Further to the connection with St Andrews, Foster, op. cit., p. 25, notes that the Liber Vitae Dunelmensis contains, within the list of those prayed for, the names of three Pictish kings: Unust, C
1 CONC ustantin and Uoenan; who can be taken as this Óengus, his putative grandson or grandnephew Caustantín and Caustantín's son Eógan. Onomastically, see works discussing Leitnamen (English: Leading names) in Medieval times, e.g. UNIQ4
