0 @N6000000002188314150@ NOTE Frithuwald of Bernicia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Frithuwald of Bernicia ruled from 579 to 585. He was the sixth known ruler of the Anglo-Saxon kingdom of Bernicia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Frithuwald was the son of Ida of Bernicia, founder of the kingdom of Bernicia. Nothing is known of Frithuwald's life and reign. The earliest authorities differ widely on the order and the regnal years of the kings between the deat
1 CONC h of Ida and the beginning of Æthelfrith's rule in 592/593.
0 @N6000000002188314160@ NOTE Hussa of Bernicia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hussa ruled from 585 to 592 and was the seventh known ruler of the Anglo-Saxon kingdom of Bernicia.
1 CONT
1 CONT It is not entirely certain whether Hussa was the son of Ida, founder of the kingdom of Bernicia, or rather the leader of a rival Anglian faction. Little is known of Hussa's life and reign, however. At some point during his reign, 
1 CONC the coalition forces of Rheged and the Brythonic kingdoms of Strathclyde, Bernicia and Elmet laid siege to Hussa and was almost successful in driving the Anglian Bernician kings out of Britain. It is thought this alliance ultimate
1 CONC ly failed due to arguments between the different British tribes culminating in the murder of Urien, the king of Rheghed, around 590 by his former ally, Morcant.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nevertheless, there is some evidence from the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle that following Hussa's death, there was a schism between his family and that of Æthelfrith, Hussa's successor, for it states that Hering son of Hussa, led Áedán m
1 CONC ac Gabráin's forces against Æthelfrith at the Battle of Degsastan in 603.
1 CONT
1 CONT The years of Hussa's reign are conjecture: the earliest authorities differ widely on the order and the regnal years of the kings between the death of Ida and the beginning of Æthelfrith's rule in 592/593.
