0 @N6000000002188123086@ NOTE Eomer
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Eomer (or Eomaer) (? - c. 489) was, according to the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, the great-great-grandfather of Creoda of Mercia, the first King of Mercia. He is considered the ancestor to the Kings of Mercia. Eomer himself was the son
1 CONC  of Angeltheow. Eomer's son was Icel.
1 CONT
1 CONT His name may have been the basis for the name of the fictional character Éomer, as J. R. R. Tolkien was an avid student of the history and language of Mercia, and based many of the names of Rohan on Mercian examples[citation neede
1 CONC d].
1 CONT
1 CONT He is mentioned in lines 1958-1963 of the Anglo-Saxon epic Beowulf as the son of Offa and grandson of Garmund.
1 CONT
1 CONT     ...forþam Offa wæs
1 CONT     geofum and guðum gar-cene man,
1 CONT     wide geweorðod; wisdome heold
1 CONT     eðel sinne, þonon Eomær woc
1 CONT     hæleðum to helpe, Heminges mæg,
1 CONT     nefa Garmundes, niða cræftig.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT     ...Hence Offa was praised
1 CONT     for his fighting and feeing by far-off men,
1 CONT     the spear-bold warrior; wisely he ruled
1 CONT     over his empire. Eomer woke to him,
1 CONT     help of heroes, Hemming's kinsman,
1 CONT     Grandson of Garmund, grim in war.(Gummere's translation)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Eomer's immediate family
1 CONT     * A History of Mercia
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Angeltheow Legendary king of the Angles Succeeded by
1 CONT Icel
