0 @N6000000001353843075@ NOTE Alpin was king of the Dalriadic Scots.  The kingdom after the Romans withdrew from  Caledonia (the name the Romans called the land north ofBritannia) in 407 was divided among four tribes, three of which were Celtic, and the fourth
1 CONC   the Angles.  Those tribal divisions were the Picts, the Scots, the Britons and the Angles
0 @N6000000001354412070@ NOTE Alpin was king of the Dalriadic Scots.  The kingdom after the Romans withdrew from  Caledonia (the name the Romans called the land north ofBritannia) in 407 was divided among four tribes, three of which were Celtic, and the fourth
