0 @N6000000003051286233@ NOTE King of the Scots 834
1 CONT
1 CONT He was killed fighting the Picts.
1 CONT
1 CONT [From Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpin_II_of_Dalriada]
1 CONT Alpin II (Scottish Gaelic: Alpin mac Echdach) (died 841 in Galloway, Scotland) was king of Dál Riata from 839 until 841. He was the father of Kenneth I and Donald I.
1 CONT
1 CONT Alpin was certainly dead by 841, when his son, Kenneth, took the kingship of Dál Riata. A late source states that he died in 834 fighting the Picts in Galloway. He did not succeed to the kingship of the Picts.
0 @N6000000003635697848@ NOTE [2071] Microsoft Encarta Encyclopedia, King of the Gaelic Scots in Galloway
1 CONT
1 CONT "Bloodlines...", p 274, 279, reigned 839-41
0 @N6000000003949883529@ NOTE Since contemporary Irish annal entries clearly refer to Alpin's sons Kenneth and Donald as being sons of Alpin, his existence is quite secure.  While the scanty sources that survive represent him as having been killed while fighti
1 CONC ng in Galloway, it is certainly not true that he "is usually presumed to be a sub king of Galloway."  The available sources are far too slim to make such a rash statement, and many historians sensibly avoid jumping to conclusions 
1 CONC like that.  If you want information on the early Scottish kings, you should go to   Marjorie O. Anderson's "Kings & Queens of early Scotland" 
0 @N6000000006348209267@ NOTE Weis gives an additional 11 generations of the ancestors of Alpin.
