1 CONC  Dee, in proof of his fealty. Gwaethvoed, inanswer to his summons, said he could not row, and that he would not,if he could, except it were to save a person's life, whether king orvassal. Edgar sent a second and very imperious mes
1 CONC sage, whichGwaethvoed did not seem at all to notice, until the messenger beggedto know what reply he should deliver to the king; when Gwaethevoed, inthe Welsh language, answered thus: 'Say to him, fear him who fears notdeath.: Thi
1 CONC s stern reply, discovering at once to Edgar the fearlessunbending character he had to deal with, he prudently changed hisautocratic decree into a desire of mutual friendship, and going toGwaethvoed, gave the chief his hand in pled
1 CONC ge of his sincerity.Gwaethvoed married Morfydd, one of the daughters and co-heirs of Ivor,king or lord of Gwent. [Burke's Commoners III:387]
