0 @N6000000001540848590@ NOTE Ealhswith
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Ealhswith
1 CONT Queen of the Anglo-Saxons[dubious ? discuss] (more...)
1 CONT Consort 23 April 871 ? 26 October 899
1 CONT Consort to Alfred the Great
1 CONT Issue
1 CONT Ælfthryth
1 CONT Ethelfleda
1 CONT Ethelgiva
1 CONT Edward the Elder
1 CONT Æthelwærd
1 CONT Royal house House of Wessex
1 CONT Father Æthelred Mucil
1 CONT Born c. 852
1 CONT Mercia
1 CONT Died 5 December 905 (aged 53)
1 CONT
1 CONT Burial St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester
1 CONT Occupation Nun
1 CONT Ealhswith (or Ealswitha) of the Gaini was born c. 852 in Mercia. Her name means "Temple strength".
1 CONT
1 CONT Her father was Æthelred Mucil, Ealdorman of the Gaini. She was married in 868, to Alfred the Great, king of Wessex. The children of Alfredand Ealhswith included Edward the Elder, later king of Wessex, Ælfthryth, who married Baldwi
1 CONC n II, Count of Flanders, and Ethelfleda, who ruled as Lady of the Mercians.
1 CONT
1 CONT After Alfred's death in 899, Ealhswith became a nun. She died on 5 December 905, and is buried in St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester, Hampshire.
1 CONT
1 CONT Also ref. History of the Anglo-Saxons (1831) by Sir Francis Palgrave for more details on her husband Alfred the Great.
0 @N6000000000604974206@ NOTE Ethelswitha, Princess of Mercia1 (F) d. 5 December 905, #102607Pedigree <JavaScript:pup('Ethelswitha, Princess of Mercia|d. 5 Dec 905|p10261.htm> Last Edited=24 Sep 2003
1 CONT Ethelswitha, Princess of Mercia was the daughter of Ethelred Mucel, Ealdorman of the Gainas <p10263.htm> and Edburga (?) , Princess of Mercia <p10646.htm>.1 She married Alfred 'the Great', King of Wessex, son of Ethelwulf, King of
1 CONC  Wessex and Osburga (?), between 868 and 869.1 She died on 5 December 905 at Winchester, Hampshire, England.1 She was buried at St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester, Hampshire, England.1  She was also known as Elswitha (?). She gained the
1 CONC  title of Princess Ethelswitha of Mercia. She was a nun circa 901 at St. Mary's Abbey, Winchester, Hampshire.1
1 CONT Children of Ethelswitha, Princess of Mercia and Alfred 'the Great', King of Wessex:
1 CONT Ethelgiva (?) <p10263.htm> d. c 896 Elfrida (?) <p10263.htm>+ d. 7 Jun 929 Ethelfleda, Lady of Mercia <p10263.htm>+ b. c 869, d. 12 Jun 918 Edmund (?) <p10647.htm> b. c 870 Edward 'the Elder', King of Wessex <p10244.htm>+ b. c 871
1 CONC , d. 17 Jul 924 Ethelweard (?) <p10263.htm>+ b. c 880, d. bt 920 - 922
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S11 <s1.htm>] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 9. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
