1 CONC ess, and all their horses which they had brought with them out of France, and leaving behind them in the fortress the greater part of their prisoners, on the arrival of the king, fled immediately to their ships, and the Saxons imm
1 CONC ediately seized on the prisoners and horses left by the pagans; and so the pagans, compelled by stern necessity, returned the same summer [885] to France."  According to Æthelweard, not all of these raiders left Britain. He says: 
