1 CONT [Brit. Enc.] king of Wessex 871-899.  [ Pat(ricia) Boren,  pboren - at -
1 CONT rand.org]:  An email pal sent me a  copy of some charts from 'Ancestral
1 CONT Peregrinations' by Richard B.  McConnell.  The front page of the copy
1 CONT (which was a second printing by  Charles Fleetwood  in 1979) says, 'This
1 CONT charming and interesting work pertained to the BOHUN  family of England
1 CONT and South Carolina...very limited edition of 100  copies.' I'll be
1 CONT posting several lines of descent that I'd like comments  on and
1 CONT verification.  The sources include:  JW:  Magna Carta by John  Wurts.
1 CONT CC:  Royal Ancestors of Magna Carta Barons by Carr P. Collins.  FW:
1 CONT Ancestral Roots (1950s edition).  Of course, these are secondary sources,
1 CONT dating about 1955. Anyway, here's  the first I'd like yeps or nopes
1 CONT about.
1 CONT 1.  Alfred the Great = Lady Alswitha.
1 CONT 2.  Lady Ethelfreda = Ethelred, earl of Mercia (son of Hugh the earl of
1 CONT Mercia).
1 CONT 3.  Lady Elfwina = Edulf (son of Ordgar, earl of Devon).
1 CONT 4.  Leofwine = Lady Alward (dau of Athelstan, the Danish duke of East
1 CONT Anglia).
1 CONT 5.  Leofric = Lady Godiva (dau of the Earl of Lincoln). //  [Alan Wilson
