1 CONC D:  Genealogical Publishing Co, 1995), p. 2
1 CONT
1 CONT King of England 899-924.
1 CONT He defeated the Danes (918), taking East Anglia, and also conquered Mercia
1 CONT (918) and Northumbria (920).
0 @N6000000000437150019@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> King Name Suffix:<NSFX> I, King Of Wessex "The Elder" Kingof England from 899-924.  A solider trained by his father, Alfred, who was able to greatly spread English influence over the Danes, Scots, Britons (in Wa
1 CONC les)and in Europe.  Some believe that his eldest son, Athelstan, was actually theson of a mistress.@S157@S166@
