0 @N6000000002329577568@ NOTE Edward the Elder
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT (Redirected from Edward I the Elder of England)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Edward the Elder [Ed Elder.jpg]
1 CONT
1 CONT Rank: 7th
1 CONT
1 CONT Ruled: October 26, 899-July 17, 924
1 CONT
1 CONT Predecessor: Alfred the Great
1 CONT
1 CONT Date of Birth: 871
1 CONT
1 CONT Place of Birth: Wessex, England
1 CONT
1 CONT Wives: Egwina, Elfleda, and Edgiva
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried: Winchester Cathedral
1 CONT
1 CONT Date of Death: July 17, 924
1 CONT
1 CONT Parents: Alfred and Ealhswith
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT King Edward the Elder was born in about 871 AD, the son of King Alfred the Great. He became King of Wessex on his father's death in 899, and exceeded Alfred's military achievements, restoring the Danelaw to Saxon rule and reigning
1 CONC  in Mercia 
1 CONT from 918, after the death of his sister, Ethelfleda. He spent his early reign fighting his cousin Aethelwald, son of Ethelred I. He had about eighteen children from his three marriages, and may have had an illegitimate child, too.
1 CONC  He died in
1 CONT about 924, and was buried at Winchester . This portrait is imaginary and was drawn together with portraits of other Anglo-Saxons monarchs by an unknown artist on the 18th century.
0 @N6000000002187592404@ NOTE Edward the Elder
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Edward I the Elder 
1 CONT King of Wessex 
1 CONT
1 CONT Reign 26 October 899 - 17 July 924 
1 CONT Coronation 8 June 900, Kingston upon Thames 
1 CONT Born c.871 
1 CONT  Wessex, England 
1 CONT Died 17 July 924 
1 CONT  Farndon-on-Dee, Cheshire England 
1 CONT Buried New Minster, Winchester, later translated to Hyde Abbey 
1 CONT Predecessor Alfred the Great and
1 CONT Ethelfleda, Lady of the Mercians 
1 CONT Successor Ælfweard of Wessex and
1 CONT Athelstan of England 
1 CONT Consort Ecgwynn, Ælfflæd, and Edgiva 
1 CONT Father Alfred the Great 
1 CONT Mother Ealhswith 
1 CONT
1 CONT Edward I the Elder (Old English: Eadweard se Ieldra) (c. 871 – 17 July 924) was King of England (899 – 924). He was the son of Alfred the Great (Ælfred se Greata) and Alfred's wife, Ealhswith, and became King of Wessex upon his fa
1 CONC ther's death in 899.
