0 @N6000000001956325405@ NOTE
1 CONT King of England and Wessex, King of Angles and Saxons Edward The Elder Anglo-Saxon king in England, the son of Alfred the Great. As ruler of the West Saxons, or Wessex, from 899 to 924, Edward extended his authority over almost al
1 CONC l of England by conquering areas that previously hadbeen held by Danish invaders.
1 CONT Edward ascended the throne upon his father's death in October 899, and in a battle in 902 his forces killed a rival claimant, Aethelwald, who had allied with the Danes. After defeating the Northumbrian Danes at Tettenhall, he set 
1 CONC out in August 912 to subdue the Danes of the eastern Midlands and East Anglia. From 910 to 916 he constructed a series of fortified enclosures around his Kingdom of Wessex.
1 CONT At the same time, his sister, the Mercian ruler Aethelflaed, constructed a complementaryseries of fortresses in the northwest Midlands. In 917 Edward and Aethelflaed launched a massive offensive, quickly overwhelming the entire Da
1 CONC nish army of East Anglia. Upon Aethelflaed's death in June 918, Edward assumed control of Mercia, and by the end of the year the last Danish armies in the Midlands had submitted. By that time Edward's kingdom included all the land
1 CONC  south of the Humber estuary; in 920 he pacified Northumbria. Complete political unification of England was achieved during the reign ofhis son and successor, Athelstan (reigned 924-939).
