1 CONT King of Wessex (899-924).  He fought with his father against the Danes and was
1 CONT apparently joint king with him.  He gradually became ruler of all England
1 CONT south of the Humber. - Encyclopedia, p 254
1 CONT Had children by his concubine Ecgwyna and contracted a legitimate marriage
1 CONT only after the death of his father ... subsequently married twice, probably
1 CONT repudiating one wife - Marriage and the Family in the Middle Ages, p. 106
1 CONT EDWARD THE ELDER, son of ALFRED THE GREAT and EALHSWITH, ...was so handicapped by an unruly temper and ungoverned speech that many of the nobility would have preferred Ethelred for their king.
1 CONT  Edward was duly crowned, and in his brief reign, troubled
1 CONT by divided opinion, some of the monasteries which had been enriched and enlarged under his pious father and Dunstan's influence were stripped of their recent endowment by neighbouring landowners who
1 CONT  may have distrusted the growing influence of the
1 CONT church, and
1 CONT certainly resented the late diminishment of their own importance ... Three years after his accession, Ewad was murdered, at Corfe in Dorset, where he had gone to visit his stepmother and his
1 CONT  half-brother Ethelred.  It was the 18th March, and in the
1 CONT evening he rode back, after hunting, and outside the castle was surrounded by men of the household.  A cry escapes that impenetrable scene - 'What do ye, breaking my right arm?' - and the young king,
1 CONT  still upon his horse, was stabbed to death at the
1 CONT instigation of unknown conspirators.
1 CONT Ethelred was too young to have been involved, and there is no evidence that his mother was implicated.  But Edward was buried without royal honours, and no one was punished for his death, though the
1 CONT  Chronicle declares that 'no worse deed than this for
1 CONT the English people was committed since first they came to Britain.' Edward, the unruly boy, got a martyr's fame, and his tomb inspired a legend of the miracles wrought above it; while Ethelred was
1 CONT  crowned king an an air that was heavy with suspicion -
