1 CONT The Ango-Saxon form of his name is Eadweard.  This Edward, the son of Alfred, is known as Edward the Elder.  His reign was from 901 to 924. He was buried beside his father at Winchester, in the "New
1 CONT  Minster" which Alfred had begun and which he himself
1 CONT finished.  - A Short History of England, Edward P. Cheyney, p. 69
