1 CONT DATA
1 CONT TEXT Date of Import: Oct 20, 19992nd gen. desc. of Alfred 'The Great' of Britain.  Acceded to the throne upon the death of Alfred 'The Great' in 899.  In 910, he defeated the Danes at the Battle of
1 CONT  Tettenhall and advanced into portions of East Anglia, the Midlands, and Essex.  Defeated the Danes in 918 where he took East Anglia; conquered Mercia in 918; acknowledged by the princes of West
1 CONT  Wales as overlord in 919; and conquered portions of Northumbria in 920. His son, Athelstan, becomes King of all England upon his death in 925.
1 CONT ------------
1 CONT Edward the Elder (died 924), king of Wessex (899-924), son of King Alfred. He succeeded as king of the Angles and Saxons in 899, despite a rebellion led by his cousin Ethelwald with the support of
1 CONT  the Danes of Northumbria and East Anglia. After a protracted struggle he defeated the Danes, and in 912, on the death of his brother-in-law Ethelred, alderman of Mercia, he annexed the cities of
1 CONT  London and Oxford and their environs.  The Danes submitted formally in 918, and soon thereafter the sovereignty of Edward was acknowledged by the North Welsh, the Scots, the Northumbrians, and the
1 CONT  Welsh of Strathclyde. Edward was succeeded by his son Athelstan.
1 CONT Source: "Edward the Elder," Microsoft(R) Encarta(R) 98 Encyclopedia. (c) 1993-1997 Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.
1 CONT
