1 CONT GIVN Edward "The Elder" King of
1 CONT SURN ENGLAND
1 CONT DATE 15 Dec 2000
1 CONT HIST: @N487@
1 CONT
1 CONT HIST ACCEDED TO THE THRONE UPON THE DEATH OF ALFRED THE GREAT IN 899.
1 CONT HIST IN 912, DEFEATED THE DANES AT THE BATTLE OF TETTANHALL AND ADVANCED ONTO EAST ANGLIA.  DEFEATED THE DANES IN 918, TOOK MERCIA, CONQUERED PORTIONS OF NORTHUMBRIA IN 920.
1 CONT HIST AETHELSTAN SUCCEEDS HIM AFTER HIS DEATH IN 925
1 CONT DATE 22 MAY 2000Sources: RC 233, 261, 321, 359, 376; Coe; A. Roots 1-16, 1 6, 45; AF; Warrior
1 CONT Kings; Shorter History of England; Through the Ages; K and Q of Britain;
1 CONT Pfafman; Kraentzler 1470, 1475, 1631; Kirby; Young; Magna Charta Sureties
1 CONT 161-2.
1 CONT Edward was a Bretwala (King of Kings). First King of all Eng land. Ruled from
1 CONT 899-924. K&Q says from 899-925. Several daughters became nuns .
1 CONT K: Edward I, "The Pious."
1 CONT Roots: Edward the Elder, Saxon King of England, m arried (2) Alfflaed, (3)
1 CONT Eadgifu.
1 CONT Sureties: Edward I, the Elder, King of Engl and 901-924. Born 875 and died
1 CONT 924.
1 CONT Kirby: Eadweard.
1 CONT Young: Edward the Elder , died 924, King of England and overlord of the Welsh
1 CONT princes.
1 CONT Warrior Kings: "Edward, eldest son, was a warrior rather than a scholar,
1 CONT though in this capa city he probably took a good deal of weight from his
1 CONT father's shoulders. The r elationship between father and son seems to have been
1 CONT amicable."Dead
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: King of England from 899-924. A solider trained by his father, Alfred, who was able to greatly spread English influence over the Danes, Scots, Britons (in Wales) and in Europe. Some believe that his eldest son, Athelstan, wa
1 CONC s actually the son of a mistress.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Dead
