0 @N6000000000232618302@ NOTE ==========
1 CONT
1 CONT Ælfthryth, Countess of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ælfthryth, also known as Elfrida, (died 929), was the last child of Alfred the Great, the Saxon King of England and his wife Ealhswith. She had four or five siblings, including King Edward the Elder and Ethelfleda.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ælfthryth married Baldwin II (d. 918), Count of Flanders. One of their descendants, Matilda of Flanders (d. 1083), would go on to marry William the Conqueror, therefore starting the Anglo-Norman line of Kings of England. Through h
1 CONC er descendant, Henry I of England, she is also a direct ancestor of the current monarch of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, Elizabeth II.
1 CONT
1 CONT ==========
0 @N6000000000269777572@ NOTE Aelfthryth, also known as Elfrida, (d. 929), was the last child of Alfred the Great, the Saxon King of England and his wife Ealhswith. She had four or five siblings, including Edward the Elder and Ethelfleda.
1 CONT
1 CONT Aelfthryth married Baldwin II (d. 918), Count of Flanders. One of their descendants, Matilda of Flanders (d. 1083), would go on to marry William the Conqueror, therefore starting the Anglo-Norman line of Kings of England. Through 
1 CONC her descendant, Henry I of England, she is also a direct ancestor of the current monarch of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, Elizabeth II.
