1 CONT He died 995, Finela's Castle, Fettercain.  King of Alba and said thathave married a princes s of Leinster. "He began his reign by ravaging theBritons, probably as an act of vengeance, b ut his name is also includedamong a group of
1 CONC  northern and western kings said to have made sub missionto the Anglo-Saxon king Edgar in 973, perhaps at Chester; and thechronicler Roger of W endover (Flores Historiarum, under the year 975)states that shortly afterward Kenneth 
1 CONC receive d from Edgar all the landcalled Lothian (i.e., between the Tweed and the Forth rivers). Thi s isthe first mention of the River Tweed as the recognized border betweenEngland and Scotland . Kenneth was slain, apparently by h
1 CONC is own subjects,at Fettercairn in the Mearns." Britannic a Online
