0 @N6000000002187592460@ NOTE Ethelweard
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ethelweard
1 CONT King of England
1 CONT Reign July 17, 924 - August 2, 924
1 CONT Born circa 904
1 CONT Wessex
1 CONT Died August 2, 924
1 CONT Buried Winchester Cathedral
1 CONT Married Never married
1 CONT Parents Edward the Elder
1 CONT Elfleda
1 CONT
1 CONT Ethelweard or Æðelweard (904 – 924) was son of Edward the Elder. According to one version of the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, Æðelweard (a bookish boy) was appointed king.
1 CONT
1 CONT Supposedly, he became a hermit at Bridgnorth, and was elected king by the witan after his father's death. He died in Oxford after being king for only sixteen days. Some say that he was assassinated upon the orders of his half-brot
1 CONC her Æðelstan. He was buried at Winchester.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Edward the Elder King of England
1 CONT 924 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Athelstan
