0 @N6000000002187592441@ NOTE Edred of England
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Edred
1 CONT King of England  
1 CONT Reign May 26, 946 - November 23, 955 
1 CONT Born 923
1 CONT Wessex, England 
1 CONT Died November 23, 955
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried Winchester Cathedral 
1 CONT Married Never married 
1 CONT Parents Edward the Elder
1 CONT Edgiva 
1 CONT King Edred or Eadred (c. 923 – 23 November 955) was King of England from 946 until his death. He was a son of King Edward the Elder by his third marriage, to Edgiva, daughter of Sigehelm, Ealdorman of Kent. He succeeded his brothe
1 CONC r, King Edmund I. Like both his elder brothers, Edred enjoyed military success over the Vikings. However, Edred was a strongly religious man but in very poor health (he could barely eat his food). He died on November 23, 955, at F
1 CONC rome in Somerset, and was buried at Winchester. He was succeeded by his nephew, King Edwy.
0 @N6000000002322323967@ NOTE Edred's brother, in 954, became immediate lord of York and Yorkshire, after
1 CONT a succession of ephemeral kings of Norse origin can be traced at York,
1 CONT disappearing in that year of 954. The added territories were passed onto
1 CONT Edred and future English kings. Edred left no immediate heirs, only two young
1 CONT nephews: Eadwig and Edgar. Eadwig succeeded his uncle Edred.
0 @N6000000002176666848@ NOTE Edred's brother, in 954, became immediate lord of York and Yorkshire, after
