1 CONT disappearing in that year of 954. The added territories were passed onto
1 CONT Edred and future English kings. Edred left no immediate heirs, only two young
1 CONT nephews: Eadwig and Edgar. Eadwig succeeded his uncle Edred.
0 @N6000000002240810967@ NOTE Edred's brother, in 954, became immediate lord of York and Yorkshire, after
1 CONT a succession of ephemeral kings of Norse origin can be traced at York,
1 CONT disappearing in that year of 954. The added territories were passed onto
1 CONT Edred and future English kings. Edred left no immediate heirs, only two young
1 CONT nephews: Eadwig and Edgar. Eadwig succeeded his uncle Edred.
0 @N6000000002244413782@ NOTE Edred's brother, in 954, became immediate lord of York and Yorkshire, after
1 CONT a succession of ephemeral kings of Norse origin can be traced at York,
1 CONT disappearing in that year of 954. The added territories were passed onto
