1 CONT nephews: Eadwig and Edgar. Eadwig succeeded his uncle Edred.
0 @N6000000004533104170@ NOTE Eadred was the first king to rule all of England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Eadred, also spelled EDRED (d. 23 Nov 955, Frome, in modern Somerset,England), king of the English from 946 to 955, who brought Northumbriapermanently under English rule.  Eadred was the son of the West Saxonking Edward the Elder 
1 CONC (ruled 899-924), the half brother of KingAthelstan (ruled 924-939), and the brother of King Edmund I (ruled939-946).  Upon Eadred's accession to power, the Northumbriansacknowledged his overlordship, but they soon proclaimed as th
1 CONC eir kingErik Bloodax, son of the Norwegian ruler Harald I Fairhair.  Inrevenge Eadred ravaged all of Northumbria (948).  The Northumbrianssubmitted to Eadred, but in 949 they accepted another Norse king, OlafSihtricson, as their r
1 CONC uler.  They overthrew Olaf in 952 in favour ofErik Bloodax, who in turn was expelled and killed in 954.  TheNorthumbrians then resumed their allegiance to Eadred.
1 CONT
1 CONT Eadred was a close friend of Dunstan, abbot of Glastonbury (laterarchbishop of Canterbury), and a supporter of the monastic revivalinspired by Dunstan.  [Encyclopaedia Britannica]
0 @N6000000007329573457@ NOTE [Kopi av ROYALS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Succeded the throne of his brother, Edmund I the Elder.
1 CONT Reign: 946 - 955.
