0 @N6000000002187592351@ NOTE Edmund I of England
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund I
1 CONT King of England  
1 CONT Reign October 27, 939 – May 26, 946 
1 CONT Born 921
1 CONT Wessex, England 
1 CONT Died May 26, 946
1 CONT
1 CONT Buried Glastonbury Abbey 
1 CONT Married Elgiva and Ethelfleda 
1 CONT Parents Edward the Elder
1 CONT Edgiva of Kent 
1 CONT Edmund I, or Edmund the Deed-Doer (Eadmund) (921–May 26, 946) was King of England from 939 until his death. He was a son of Edward the Elder and half-brother of Athelstan.
1 CONT
1 CONT Athelstan died on October 27, 939, and Edmund succeeded him as King. Shortly after his proclamation as king he had to face several military threats. King Olaf I of Dublin conquered Northumbria and invaded the Midlands. When Olaf d
1 CONC ied in 942 Edmund reconquered the Midlands. In 943 he became the god-father of King Olaf of York. In 944, Edmund was successful in reconquering Northumbria. In the same year his ally Olaf of York lost his throne and left for Dubli
1 CONC n in Ireland. Olaf became the king of Dublin as Olaf Cuaran and continued to be allied to his god-father. In 945 Edmund conquered Strathclyde but conceded his rights on the territory to King Malcolm I of Scotland. In exchange they
1 CONC  signed a treaty of mutual military support. Edmund thus established a policy of safe borders and peaceful relationships with Scotland. During his reign, the revival of monasteries in England began.
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund was murdered in 946 by Leofa, an exiled thief. He had been having a party in Pucklechurch, when he spotted Leofa in the crowd. After the outlaw refused to leave, the king and his advisors fought Leofa. Edmund and Leofa were
1 CONC  both killed. He was succeeded as king by his brother Edred, king from 946 until 955.
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund's sons later ruled England as:
1 CONT
1 CONT Edwin of England, King from 955 until 957, king of only Wessex and Kingdom of Kent from 957 until his death on October 1, 959. 
1 CONT Edgar of England, king of only Mercia and Northumbria from 957 until his brother's death in 959, then king of England from 959 until 975. 
1 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT King of the English 939 - 946. Edmund was stabbed at a banquet - according to some historians, by Leolf, an outlaw. Source: RoyaList, Leo van de Pas 
