1 CONT BAOSE.TAF (Compuserve)
1 CONT
1 CONT Succeeded his brother Athelstan; Killed while defending his steward against a criminal who had returned from banishment - Anglo-Saxon England, Sir Frank Stenton, p. 360; Born about 921; According to COMYN4.TAF (Compuserve Roots) h
1 CONC is mother was Edgive (possibly another spelling for his father's concubine), but the dates don't seem to work - NLP
