1 CONT AFN: GS4H-RK
0 @N6000000000269761346@ NOTE Baldwin II of Flanders (c. 865 \endash  September 10, 918), nicknamed Calvus (the Bald) was the second count of Flanders. He was also hereditary abbot of St. Bertin from 892 till his death. He was the son of Baldwin I of Flanders 
1 CONC and Judith, a daughter of Charles the Bald.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] History
1 CONT The early years of Baldwin's rule were marked by a series of devastating Viking raids. Little north of the Somme was untouched. Baldwin recovered, building new fortresses and improving city walls, and taking over abandoned propert
1 CONC y, so that in the end he held far more territory, and held it more strongly, than had his father. He also took advantage of the conflicts between Charles the Simple and Odo, Count of Paris to take over the Ternois and the Boulonni
1 CONC as.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 884 Baldwin married Aelfthryth (Ælfthryth, Elftrude, Elfrida), a daughter of King Alfred the Great of England. The marriage was motivated by the common Flemish-English opposition to the Vikings, and was the start of an alliance
1 CONC  that was a mainstay of Flemish policy for centuries to come.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 900, he tried to curb the power of Archbishop Fulk of Rheims by assassinating him, but he was excommunicated by Pope Benedict IV.
1 CONT
1 CONT He died at Blandimberg and was succeeded by his eldest son Arnulf I of Flanders. His younger son Adalulf was (the first) count of Boulogne.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT He married Aelfthryth, a daughter of Alfred the Great, King of England. They had the following:
1 CONT
1 CONT Arnulf I of Flanders (c.890-964), married Adela of Vermandois 
1 CONT Adalulf (c.890-933), Count of Boulogne 
1 CONT Ealswid 
1 CONT Ermentrud 
1 CONT His fifth child however, was illegitimate.
1 CONT
1 CONT Albert (d.977) 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT Annales Blandinienses 
1 CONT Folcwine, Gesta Abbatum S. Bertini Sithiensium
0 @N6000000000437066884@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Count Name Suffix:<NSFX> II, Of Flanders "The Bald" "BALDWIN THE BALD, French BAUDOUIN LE CHAUVE, Dutch BOUDEWIJN DE KALE, second ruler of Flanders, who, from his stronghold at Bruges, maintained, as his father 
1 CONC Baldwin I before him, a vigorous defense of his lands against the incursions of theNorsemen. On his mother's side a descendant of Charlemagne, he strengthened thedynastic importance of his family by marrying Aelfthryth, daughter o
1 CONC f Alfred the Great, of Wessex, Eng."@S169@
