0 @N6000000003219704343@ NOTE He died on 27 Mar 964 in or March 27, 966.  Arnulf was preoccupied with fighting off the Northmen. "In his old age he placed the government in the hands of Baldwin, his son by Adela, daughter of the count of Vermandois, and the yo
1 CONC ung man in a short reign did much for the commercial and industrial progress of the country, setting up the first weavers and fullers at Ghent, and instituting yearly fairs at Ypres, Bruges and other places. On Baldwin III's death
1 CONC  in 961 the old count resumed control and spent the few remaining years of his life in securing the succession of his grandson Arnulf II...."{Encycl.Brit., 1956, 9:356} (source: Albert E. Meyers database, aem@ezonline.com,hhttp://
1 CONC www.ezonline.com/aem/aem.html)
1 CONT
1 CONT ARNULF, of Flanders, the Forester, who died in 988
