0 @N6000000002176669368@ NOTE Wessex, early Anglo-Saxon kingdom in southern England east of Cornwall, was
1 CONT founded by 2 princes, Cerdic and son Cynric in 494 or 495. Settlers followed
1 CONT in 501 and 514. They became kings in 519 in the southern part of Hampshire
1 CONT after successive battles with the Welsh. In 530, they conquered the Isle of
1 CONT Wight, which they gave to 2 relatives, Stuf and Wihgar. This dynasty is
1 CONT claimed to be of the same origin as the house of Benicia. When Cerdic died in
1 CONT 534, son Cynric succeeded, followed by his son, Ceawlin in 560.
