0 @N6000000002248115786@ NOTE Cerdic, King of the West Saxons, 519-534, was a Saxon earldorman who founded a settlement on the coast of Hampshire, England, in 495, assumed the title of King of the West Saxons in 519, and became the ancestor of the English roya
1 CONC l line.  "A. D. 495.  This year came two leaders into Britain, Cerdic and Cynric, his son, with five ships...519.  This year Cerdic and Cynric undertook the government ot the West Saxons; the same year they fought with the Britons
1 CONC  at a place called Charford.   From that day have reigned the children of the West Saxon kings.  530.  They conquered the isle of Wight...534.  This year died Cerdic, the first king of the West Saxons.  Cynric his son succeded to 
1 CONC the government, and reigned afterwards twenty-six winters."
