1 CONC f Elmet in the early seventh century. Whatever may be the implications - and the possibilities are manifold - the presence of this anomalous name in the genealogies did not embarrass those who claimed to be his descendants: 'his k
1 CONC in goes back to Cerdic' was a regular boast of the chroniclers who recorded the doings of later kings of Wessex.
