1 CONC cord of the early Anglo-Saxon period confirms that this region was one nucleus of the later kingdom of Wessex. Archaeology reveals much thicker Germanic settlement of the upper Thames valley, notably round Dorchester-on-Thames whi
1 CONC ch was later, significantly, to be the site of the first West Saxonbishopric under Birinus; but on the early traditions of this region the literary sources are silent. It is a reminder (if one were needed) that the origins of the 
1 CONC political entity later known as the kingdom of Wessex were more complex and diverse than we shall ever know.
