0 @N6000000002322288513@ NOTE Posthumous son of Louis II, he was cousin to Charles the Fat, King of France
1 CONT 884-887. He was generally recognized as king on the death of King Eudes in
1 CONT 898. His authority came to be accepted by Lorraine and he settled the
1 CONT Northmen in Normandy but became the first Caolingian ruler of the western
1 CONT kingdom to lose his crown by alienating the nobles of Neustria. They deposed
1 CONT him by electing Robert I king. Charles killed Robert in battle in 923 but was
1 CONT taken prisoner to use against the new king, Rudolph, Robert's son-in-law.
