1 CONT Charles the Simple, ruled 893-923, was son of Louis II and joint king with Eudes, count of Paris, until 898. He ceded (911) part of Normandy to the Norse leader Rollo and was defeated and imprisoned (923) by nobles who made Raoul 
1 CONC of Burgundy king. - Encyclopedia, p. 157
1 CONT
