1 CONT LOUIS IV, son of CHARLES III and EADGIFU, ruled 936-954, was the son of King Charles III.  He spent his youth in exile in England and was recalled by the nobles under the duke Hugh the Great at the
1 CONT  death of King Raoul.  His energy and independence
1 CONT displeased Hugh, who waged war on the king but was forced to submit in 950.  Louis was succeeded by his son Lothair - Encyclopedia, p. 491
1 CONT of Laon, Aisne, France; King of France, 936-954 - Royalty for Commoners, Roderick W. Stuart, p. 130
1 CONT King CHARLES III (Charles the Simple), he was taken to England as a child by his mother Eadgifu, daughter of the Anglo-Saxon king Edward the Elder. Recalled to France to succeed King Raoul (r.
1 CONT  923-36), Louis struggled against Hugh the Great, count of
1 CONT Paris, through most of his reign. While attempting to conquer Normandy, he was captured in 945 and became Hugh's prisoner until 946. With the aid of the German king OTTO I, he eventually defeated
1 CONT  Hugh, who made peace in 950.
1 CONT He married Gerberga of Saxony. Born, circa 913[14].
