0 @N6000000003403220995@ NOTE [alfred_descendants10gen_fromrootsweb_bartont.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT the Peaceful, King of England, 959-975; m. 968, Elfrida (or Ealfthryth), b. 945; d. 1000; dau. of Earl Ordgar. (ASC 965; NSE X 165-166).
1 CONT
1 CONT The first king of a united England.  He allowed his Danish subjects to retain Danish laws.  Edgar promoted a monastic revival and encouraged trade by reforming the currency.  He improved defense by organizing coastal naval patrols
1 CONC  and a system for manning warships.  Although he suceeded on 10/1/959, he was not crowned until 973 because St. Dunstan, the Archbishop of Canterbury, disapproved of his way of life.
