0 @N6000000001540802574@ NOTE Baldwin III, Count of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT (Redirected from Baldwin III of Flanders)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT This article does not cite any references or sources. (September 2006)
1 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unverifiable material may be challenged and removed.
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin III of Flanders (940 ? January 1, 962) was count of Flanders together with his father Arnulf I.
1 CONT
1 CONT He died before his father and was succeeded by his infant son Arnulf II, with his father acting as regent until his own death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Arnulf I had made Baldwin co-ruler in 958. During his short rule, Baldwin established the weaving and fulling industry in Ghent thus layingthe basis for the economical importance of the county in the centuries to come.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 961 Baldwin married Mathilde of Burgundy, daughter of Herman, Dukeof Saxony, by whom he had a son and heir Arnulf II.
