0 @N6000000002187592942@ NOTE Baldwin III of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Baldwin III of Flanders (940 – January 1, 962) was count of Flanders together with his father Arnulf I. He died before his father and was succeeded by his infant son Arnulf II, with his father acting as regent until his own death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Arnulf I had made Baldwin co-ruler in 958. During his short rule, Baldwin established the weaving and fulling industry in Ghent thus laying the basis for the economical importance of the county in the centuries to come.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 961 Baldwin married Mathilde of Saxony, by whom he had a son and heir Arnulf II.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Arnulf I Count of Flanders
1 CONT 958 – 962
1 CONT with Arnulf I Succeeded by:
1 CONT Arnulf I 
