0 @N6000000003615386153@ NOTE Baldwin III (1130?-62), Latin king of Jerusalem (1143-62), son and successor of Fulk V the Young, count of Anjou. During much of his reign Baldwin was at war with Nur ad-Din, the Turkish ruler of Halab (Aleppo), who outmaneuvered 
1 CONC him and took Damascus in 1154. He enjoyed good relations with the Byzantine emperor Manuel I Comnenus, whose daughter he married. Baldwin was succeeded to the throne by his brother Amalric I.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT "Baldwin III," Microsoft Encarta 96 Encyclopedia.  1993-1995 Microsoft Corp.  Funk & Wagnalls Corporation.
