0 @N6000000004533059468@ NOTE I have made a general shift in dates to accomodate Godiva's (motherof Aelfgar) birth date according to Ancestral Roots and EncyclopediaBritannica.
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT The following is excerpted from a post to SGM, 23 Jun 1999, by Leo vande Pas:
1 CONT
1 CONT From: Leo van de Pas (leovdpas@iinet.net.au)
1 CONT Subject: Re: Lady Godiva
1 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval
1 CONT Date: 1999/06/23
1 CONT
1 CONT At 12:24 PM 6/23/99 -0400, you wrote:
1 CONT >Leo van de Pas wrote:
1 CONT >>
1 CONT >> The son of Leofric and Godiva :
1 CONT >>
1 CONT >> Alfgar "the Saxon", Earl of Mercia,
1 CONT >> died circa 1059/1062 was married to
1 CONT >> Elfgifu, daughter of Sigeferth and
1 CONT >> Ealdgyth.
1 CONT
1 CONT >What is the basis for this statement.  Assuming I have these names
1 CONT >right, Ealdgyth would later become wife of Edmund Ironside, andmother
1 CONT >of the exiled princes.  It has been speculated that she was daughterof
1 CONT >an earlier Ealdorman Morcar, and this would provide onomasticcontinuity
1 CONT >with the younger Ealdorman of that name.  Still, I know of no source
1 CONT >that provides any clues either to the parents of Aelfgar's wife, nor
1 CONT >that Sigeferth had a daughter.
1 CONT
1 CONT >Oops [in a slightly later post].  I left out a generation.  Thehypothesis is that Ealdgyth was
1 CONT >daughter of Aelfthryth, and maternal granddaughter of Morcar.  Thisis
1 CONT >given in Moriarty's Plantagenet Ancestry, based on an earlierhypothesis
1 CONT >(by Richardson?).  However, it does not include her having a daughterby
1 CONT >Sigeferth, or the marriage of that daughter to Aelfgar
1 CONT
1 CONT >taf [Todd A. Farmerie]
1 CONT
1 CONT Last year I bought a wonderful book "The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle"translated and edited by Michael Swanton, there are a few family treesand in this is shown that Aelfgar, Earl of East Anglia 1051-1057, Earlof Mercia 1057 was married 
1 CONC to Aelgifu, daughter of Siferth thegn ofthe Seven Boroughs (killed in 1015) and Ealdgyth (daughter ofAelfthryth) who secondly married Edmund Ironside, King of England.Aelfthryth (son of Wulfrun) is a brother of Aelfhelm, Ealdorman
1 CONC  ofNorthumbria (killed 1006) who in turn was father of Aelgifu married toCnut King of England. These genealogical pages are the last of thebook before the bibliography. I hope you have a copy otherwise wouldyou like me to photocop
1 CONC y and post?
1 CONT
1 CONT Best wishes
1 CONT
1 CONT Leo van de Pas
