0 @N6000000003796136151@ NOTE IMPERIUM
1 CONT URL: http://www.ghgcorp.com/shetler/oldimp/443.html
1 CONT Cerdic, King of Wessex
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT Born: ? 
1 CONT Died: 534 
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT Father: Elesa 
1 CONT Mother: ? 
1 CONT Married (1): ? 
1 CONT Children: 
1 CONT Cynric, King of Wessex
1 CONT Creoda 
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT King of Wessex 519-534 
1 CONT Cerdic and Cynric, two Saxon princes, came to Britain in 495, and fought with the Britons the very day they landed. In 508, they slew a British king Natanleod. In 514, the subjects of the princes arrived in Britain at what became 
1 CONC Wessex. In 519, they fought with the Britons at Charford, and in that year Cerdic assumed the government of Wessex as its first king. In 527, the two fought the Britons at Cerdic's-ley, and in 530 they conquered the Isle of Wight.
1 CONC  In 534, Cerdic died, and Cyrnic took the government. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Cerdic was given an ancestry that took him back to Woden, the chief Anglo-Saxon god. Cerdic was said to be the son of Elesa, son of Gewis, son of Wye, son of Frewin, son of Frithgar, son of Brand, son of Balday, son of Woden. For 
1 CONC Wodens own ancestors back to Adam, the first man, see Hengist, King of Kent. 
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT e-mail Joe Shetler at: shetler@ghgcorp.com 
1 CONT
1 CONT =========================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT Frederick Rose's Genealogy
