0 @N6000000002322288576@ NOTE Carolingian king, the eldest son of Louis IV. He was dominated by Hugh the
1 CONT Great and then, 956-965, by his uncle Bruno, archbishop of Cologne, whose
1 CONT support was invaluable, but who used his influence also in the interests of
1 CONT Otto I, his brother, the German king, and of Hugh Capet and other sons of
1 CONT Hugh the Great, Bruno's nephews. Note: Bruno was the great-uncle to Lothair
1 CONT and to "sons of Hugh the Great" through Edward the Elder's daughters.
