0 @N6000000001353932805@ NOTE ALIA: /Conrad "the Red," Duke of Lotharingia
1 CONT Event: Titled BET. 944 - 953 Duke of Lotharingia (Lorraine) 2
1 CONT Event: Titled Count in the Nähegau 3
1 CONT Event: Titled Count in the Speyergau 3
1 CONT Event: Titled Count in the Wormsgau 3
1 CONT Event: Titled Duke of Franconia 3
1 CONT Event: Titled Lord of Kusel and Hornbach 3
1 CONT Note:
1 CONT Conrad, also called CONRAD THE RED, German KONRAD DER ROTE (d. Aug. 10, 955, near Augsburg, Ger.), duke of Lotharingia (Lorraine) from 944 to 953 and ancestor of the Salian dynasty of German kings.
1 CONT Conrad belonged to a family of Franconian counts with rich lands in the country around Speyer and Worms. After helping King (later Emperor)Otto I suppress a rebellion of his vassals (937-939), he was given the duchy of Lotharingia
1 CONC  (944) and Otto's daughter Liudgard in marriage. Later he fell out with the king and joined Otto's son Liudolf of Swabia in a rebellion (953-954). Forced to submit, Conrad lost his duchybut not his lands in Franconia or his vassal
1 CONC s. Later reunited with the king, he fought and was killed in the Battle of Lechfeld, when the largest Hungarian army to invade German lands was destroyed. His services seem to have been decisive in securing this victory for Otto. 
1 CONC [Encyclopaedia Britannica CD '97: CONRAD]
