1 CONC ld do so if she rode naked through the crowded marketplace. She did so, with her hair covering all of her body except her legs. According to Ranulf Higden's Polychronicon, as a result Leofric freed the town from all tolls save tho
1 CONC se on horses. An inquiry made in the reign of Edward I shows that at that time no tolls were paid in Coventry except on horses. 
1 CONT
1 CONT A later account contends that Godiva required the townsmen to remain indoors at the time fixed for her ride. Peeping Tom, a citizen who looked out his window, apparently became a part of the legend in the 17th century. In most acc
1 CONC ounts he was struck blind or dead.
