1 CONC ed by his son, Osborn Fitz-Richard, or Fitz-Scrop. [Ref: John Burke, The Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, R. Bentley, London, 1834-1838, Vol. III, p. 693, Scrope, of Castle Combe
0 @N6000000004533059323@ NOTE MORTIMER of Richard's Castle
1 CONT
1 CONT The descent of the lordship of Burford, Salop, with Richard's Castle,co. Hereford, as its caput, is traced by Eyton from RICHARD FITZSCRUB,a Norman favourite of Edward the Confessor, who was allowed-by theGodwin party to remain in
