0 @N6000000000269742606@ NOTE Duncan I (1001?-40), king of Scotland (1034-40), grandson of King Malcolm II Mackenneth, whom he succeeded. Before his accession to the Scottish throne he was ruler of the kingdom of Strathclyde. Macbeth, who ruled the neighboring
1 CONC  kingdom of Moray and served Duncan as a general, killed him and became king of Scotland.
1 CONT ! Murdered by Macbeth at Bothnagowanm near Elgin
